{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794682884641,"sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d3ffe8hgDLTRt6IhrOl","part":{"partID":"prt_1db6f9025001EtESQByTfzC4Y6","sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d3ffe8hgDLTRt6IhrOl","messageID":"msg_1db6f65e7001SMVH7QShb133L3","type":"tool","id":"call_626faef5e3b645b183af97cc","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-4b/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-4b/deep-review-strategy.md, lines 1-343\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Review Strategy - accuracy-runner-confirm-4b lineage\n3: description: Runtime strategy tracking the confirming review of pass-four fixes in the accuracy-runner area of command surfacing.\n4: version: 1.11.14.0\n5: ---\n6: \n7: # Deep Review Strategy - accuracy-runner-confirm-4b lineage\n8: \n9: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n10: \n11: ### Purpose\n12: \n13: Persistent brain for this fan-out lineage. It records which dimensions remain, what was found\n14: (P0/P1/P2), which review approaches worked or failed, and where to focus next. Read at every\n15: iteration before any review action.\n16: \n17: ### Ownership\n18: \n19: Machine-managed metrics and coverage blocks are wrapped in explicit ownership anchors. Human\n20: commentary and operator overrides live outside those anchors.\n21: \n22: ---\n23: \n24: ## 2. TOPIC\n25: \n26: Confirming round of review pass four of `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`\n27: in the `accuracy-runner` area. Scope: the nine changed paths listed in\n28: `review/review-scope-4b.txt` whose area is `accuracy-runner` — the Codex session reader and its\n29: test, the routing-accuracy offer/runner pair and their tests, and the doctor presentation row —\n30: plus shared docs that describe them. The change range is `11af224a34..48f03b5013`.\n31: \n32: The operator focus is the pass-four confirming brief: read `review-brief-4b.txt` first; confirm\n33: that a refusal over an or-list and an is-the question carry no command while a request over a\n34: list keeps its command; that both run-log writers keep `offeredAs`; that a shell read of a\n35: command document counts as a start while a search, an in-place `sed`, a redirect and a heredoc\n36: line do not; that a heredoc end word with a hyphen or a dot closes correctly; that the Codex\n37: reader opens the resolved file; that the holdout guard reads the live capture; and that docs\n38: agree with code. Holdout prompt text is never read or printed.\n39: \n40: ---\n41: \n42: <!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n43: ## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n44: [All dimensions complete]\n45: \n46: <!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n47: \n48: ---\n49: \n50: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n51: \n52: - The attach module, scorer fusion, recommend handler and feature docs in the `scorer-attach`\n53:   area are the `scorer-attach-confirm-4b` lineage's scope. This lineage reads them only as\n54:   context evidence and raises no finding against them.\n55: - Holdout prompt text is never read or printed. Corpus work is limited to counts and\n56:   `jq 'del(.prompt)'` rows.\n57: - No code changes: review is observation-only.\n58: - No runtime command, build, test run or generator is executed; every claim is grounded in a\n59:   direct file read of the changed commit.\n60: \n61: ---\n62: \n63: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n64: \n65: - Convergence: `newFindingsRatio` at or below the 0.10 threshold with no active P0.\n66: - Cap: `maxIterations` 3.\n67: - Stuck: two consecutive iterations with no new evidence (stuckThreshold 2).\n68: - Any active P0 blocks PASS regardless of convergence.\n69: \n70: ---\n71: \n72: <!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n73: ## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n74: - [x] correctness\n75: - [x] security\n76: - [x] traceability\n77: - [x] maintainability\n78: \n79: <!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n80: \n81: ---\n82: \n83: <!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n84: ## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n85: - P0 (Blockers): 0\n86: - P1 (Required): 0\n87: - P2 (Suggestions): 2\n88: - Resolved: 0\n89: \n90: <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n91: \n92: ---\n93: \n94: ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n95: \n96: - Reading both writers side by side against the one reader that consumes `offeredAs` closed the\n97:   P1 question without a test run: the field is present on every path that writes a line and the\n98:   reader is the only consumer. (iteration 1)\n99: - Tracing the brief-only branch separately caught the legacy-line behavior before it was mistaken\n100:   for a dropped field. (iteration 1)\n101: - Reading the containment helper instead of the reader alone proved the Codex read lands on the\n102:   path `realpathSync` produced, and the changed test asserts both the link miss and the resolved\n103:   hit. (iteration 2)\n104: - Checking the holdout guard by row id rather than by prompt text kept the rule while proving\n105:   the G2 fixed table holds no corpus row. (iteration 2)\n106: - Comparing the README's two backfill field lists against both writers and the output-log\n107:   sentence made the stale count visible without running the harness. (iteration 3)\n108: - Following the head-moved early return showed the blanket \"every line\" sentence is false on the\n109:   one exit-3 path the README documents. (iteration 3)\n110: \n111: ---\n112: \n113: ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n114: \n115: - Nothing failed in iteration 1; the changed writer surface is four small functions and every\n116:   branch was readable directly. (iteration 1)\n117: - Two clean iterations at ratio 0.0 reached the stuck threshold, so the loop schedules a\n118:   recovery pass instead of treating the silence as convergence: dimension coverage is only 2 of 4. (iteration 2)\n119: - The recovery pass found documentation drift rather than code drift; the two P2s are in the\n120:   README that phase 027 T012/T013 edited, not in the writers themselves. (iteration 3)\n121: \n122: ---\n123: \n124: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n125: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n126: ### **A holdout row can reach a live turn through the fixed G2 table.** Ruled out by id: the G2 -- BLOCKED (iteration 2, 1 attempts)\n127: - What was tried: **A holdout row can reach a live turn through the fixed G2 table.** Ruled out by id: the G2\n128: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n129: - Do NOT retry: **A holdout row can reach a live turn through the fixed G2 table.** Ruled out by id: the G2\n130: \n131: ### **A link inside the store can escape the store.** Ruled out: `resolveInside` realpaths both -- BLOCKED (iteration 2, 1 attempts)\n132: - What was tried: **A link inside the store can escape the store.** Ruled out: `resolveInside` realpaths both\n133: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n134: - Do NOT retry: **A link inside the store can escape the store.** Ruled out: `resolveInside` realpaths both\n135: \n136: ### **The A11 row contradicts the doctor check.** Ruled out: the checker's malformed message names -- BLOCKED (iteration 3, 1 attempts)\n137: - What was tried: **The A11 row contradicts the doctor check.** Ruled out: the checker's malformed message names\n138: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n139: - Do NOT retry: **The A11 row contradicts the doctor check.** Ruled out: the checker's malformed message names\n140: \n141: ### **The backfill paragraph's \"three fields\" is correct for `--brief-only`.** Ruled out: the -- BLOCKED (iteration 3, 1 attempts)\n142: - What was tried: **The backfill paragraph's \"three fields\" is correct for `--brief-only`.** Ruled out: the\n143: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n144: - Do NOT retry: **The backfill paragraph's \"three fields\" is correct for `--brief-only`.** Ruled out: the\n145: \n146: ### **The Codex reader 