blocked approach. - Recovery note: the recovery pass changed granularity to line-level doc claims and produced the two findings.\n272: \n273: <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n274: \n275: ---\n276: \n277: ## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n278: \n279: ### Bounded Context Snapshot\n280: \n281: - Target pointers: the nine `accuracy-runner` paths in `review/review-scope-4b.txt`; the fix\n282:   commit `48f03b5013`; the verify report `review/verify-4/report.md`.\n283: - Behavior claims: `offeredAs` travels with an offer through both writers; a partner-side\n284:   command is not counted as an offer; a Codex rollout link is read at its resolved path; an A11\n285:   malformed router row is fixed by hand rather than by embed.\n286: - Reuse and conventions: the reader containment pattern already used by `claude.mjs`; the\n287:   `P0/P1/P2` scale; the delta + iteration narrative pair; the append gateway as sole state-log\n288:   writer.\n289: - Review risks and gaps: no live per-runtime session was captured in this lineage, so runtime\n290:   behaviour is read from code and tests. The scorer and corpus are a sibling lineage's surface;\n291:   this lineage reads them only to check the docs it owns.\n292: \n293: ---\n294: \n295: <!-- ANCHOR:cross-reference-status -->\n296: ## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n297: \n298: | Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n299: |----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n300: | `spec_code` | core | partial | 3 | Phase 027 T006/T007/T010/T012/T013/T017 are [x] with evidence; T012's both-field-lists claim misses the backfill paragraph and runner row. |\n301: | `checklist_evidence` | core | partial | 3 | CHK-040's two edited lists are correct; the backfill lists remain stale, and CHK-FIX-003/004 stay open with the phase. |\n302: | `skill_agent` | overlay | notApplicable | 2 | No agent definition changed in this area. |\n303: | `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | notApplicable | 2 | No runtime branch in the changed docs or writers; the Codex reader is