ch, an in-place `sed` or a heredoc line does not. A heredoc's end word may hold a hyphen or a dot.`` Verify: `rg -c -F 'read from the same reads a load is' $RA` prints 1, `rg -c -F 'may hold a hyphen or a dot' $RA` prints 1 and the em dash and semicolon count equals the one T012 printed. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS, doc-only: both sentences placed, both rg counts 1, matches readDocument and HEREDOC_BODY\n- [x] T030 Count the four fields in every sentence and name the line that carries none (`RA`). After T013. Added by T025 after the confirming round found AR4B-P2-001 and AR4B-P2-002. In the sentence that starts `` `run-command-behaviour.mjs --backfill <run-log> --out <new-log>` adds those three fields``, replace `three fields` with `four fields`. In the runner's row, replace ``rewrites a finished log with `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy` and `briefDelivered` `` with ``rewrites a finished log with `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs` and `briefDelivered` ``. Directly after the line `Each line a behaviour run appends carries four fields beside the locator, exit and changed paths:` and its list, at the end of the `briefDelivered` item, add the sentence `A line written when the head moved stops before the offer is read, so it carries none of the four and holds headMoved instead.` Verify: `rg -c 'three fields' $RAD/README.md` prints nothing, `rg -c -F 'carries none of the four' $RAD/README.md` prints 1 and `rg -c -F '`offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs` and `briefDelivered`' $RAD/README.md` prints 1. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS, doc-only: three edits, rg three fields prints nothing, the other two rg checks print 1, the head-moved sentence matches the code\n\n### Lane E: four documents\n\n- [x] T014 [P] Say that the head keeps its command (`FA`). After T003. Replace the sentence that starts ``A hub also leaves `command` off when the same command already ranks in the result`` and the sentence after it with: ``A hub below the head leaves `command` off when the same command already ranks in the result through its own command row, because `enrichCompiledRoutes()` takes the `command` fields present in the result as the commands already offered. The head keeps its command even then, because every caller renders the head and at most one partner.`` Verify: `rg -c -F 'The head keeps its command even then' $FA` prints 1, `rg -c -F 'A hub below the head leaves' $FA` prints 1, and `rg -n -F 'index === 0' $ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` prints one line. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS, doc-only: exact two-sentence replacement, both rg counts 1, index === 0 at advisor-recommend.ts:478\n- [x] T015 Correct the case count of the meaning anchor test (`FM`). After T014. In the row for `command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts`, replace `17 cases:` with `28 cases:`. Before the edit, run `rg -c -e '^\\s*it\\(' $ADV/tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts`. When it prints another number than 28, write that number in place of 28 and say so in the evidence. Verify: `rg -c -F '28 cases:' $FM` prints 1, or the printed count does, and `rg -c -F '17 cases' $FM` prints nothing. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS, doc-only: it( count 28, vitest 28 of 28, 28 cases: prints 1, 17 cases prints nothing\n- [x] T016 Name the child form on the companion line (`AR`). After T015. In the paragraph that holds `Also: /doctor:<command> <target> (<policy>)`, replace `where the policy is run, start or ask` with ``where the policy is run, start or ask, or `parent-named only` in a child session for a command the child must not start on its own``. Verify: `rg -c -F 'parent-named only' $AR` prints 1, `rg -c -F \"PARENT_NAMED_POLICY = 'parent-named only'\" $ADV/lib/render.ts` prints 1 and the em dash and semicolon count of `AR` equals its count at `BASE`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS, doc-only: parent-named only prints 1, matches policyWord and companionCommandLabel in render.ts\n- [x] T017 Name the by-hand fix for a malformed router row (`DP`). After T016. Directly below the row that starts ``| `A11` reports missing router rows``, add the row: ``| `A11` reports a malformed router row | `/doctor:agents-md embed` adds missing rows only and never rewrites one, so fix the row in `REPO RULES.md` by hand until its cell count matches the header, then run the check again |``. Verify: `rg -c -F 'reports a malformed router row' $DP` prints 1, `rg -c -F 'malformed' .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs` prints at least 1 and `DT` reports `fail 0`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS, doc-only: exact row below the A11 missing-rows row. DT printed 1220 passed 1 failed on the stale advisor dist (doctor-phrase-reach), outside this file; T018 reruns DT after the build\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n<!-- FILL: Write one verification task per requirement. Each one runs a command. GOOD: T003 Run both invocations. Verify: `ls logs/archive | wc -l` prints 3 and 10. WEAK: T003 Test everything. -->\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"acceptance-criteria.md\ndescription.json\ngoal.md\ngraph-metadata.json\nplan.md\nscratch\nspec.md\ntasks.md\n---\n---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Phase 27: review-pass-four-remediation\"\ndescription: \"Ordered worker-sized tasks that carry a decline lead over an or-list, read the article before a questioned command, keep offeredAs in both run-log writers, count a shell read of a command document as a start, fix the heredoc end word, the Codex read path, the live holdout guard and five documents, then rescore every stored arm, restate each moved start figure, run a confirming review and write the pass-four synthesis.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"review pass four remediation tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.4 -->\n# Tasks: Phase 27: review-pass-four-remediation\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n<!-- FILL: Keep the prefix table and add the two shell variables this task list uses. GOOD: `R` is `scripts/rotate-logs.sh`. `A` is `logs/archive/`. WEAK: Variables are defined below. -->\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n| `[C]` | Coordinator task: a gate, a full-suite run, a capture, a summary over the stored sessions, a probe run, a commit, a review round or the close-out. No worker runs it |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n\nEvery command runs from the repository root unless a task says `in ADV` or `in SKR`. Set the path names once with `export ADV=.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime RAD=.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy SKR=.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime SR=.skilled/hooks/shared PK=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build RL=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch PH=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation SP=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/scratch PRB=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/verify-4/probes` and run `unset OPENCODE_DB`, as the Measured Behavior block ran.\n- `G` is `git -c core.fsmonitor=false`. `BASE` is the commit T001 records and `FIX` the one T023 records. `TSX` is `--import ./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/node_modules/tsx/dist/loader.mjs`.\n- `CA` is `$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts` and `CAT` is `$ADV/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`. `CO` is `$RAD/command-offer.mjs` and `COT` is `$ADV/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts`. `R` is `$RAD/run-command-behaviour.mjs` and `CBG` is `$ADV/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts`. `S` is `$RAD/score-command-transcripts.mjs` and `CTS` is `$ADV/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts`. `CR` is `$SR/session-readers/codex.mjs` and `CRT` is `$SR/tests/session-readers/codex.test.mjs`. `SL` is `$ADV/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts`.\n- `RA` is `$RAD/README.md`, `AR` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md`, `FA` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md`, `FM` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md` and `DP` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt`.\n- `FILES` is the sixteen files above: `CA`, `CAT`, `CO`, `COT`, `R`, `CBG`, `S`, `CTS`, `CR`, `CRT`, `SL`, `RA`, `AR`, `FA`, `FM` and `DP`.\n- `VX <file>` is `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run <file>` in `ADV`. `VALL` is `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run` in `ADV`, which must report 0 failed. `TC` is `npm run typecheck` in `ADV`, which must exit 0. `BUILD` is `npm run build` in `ADV`, which must exit 0, because the CLI and both captures load the compiled `dist`. `RT` is `node --test $SR/tests/session-readers/*.test.mjs`, which must report `fail 0`. `HT` is `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run tests/history-lookup-cli.vitest.ts tests/history-lookup-adapters-e2e.vitest.ts` in `SKR`, which must report 0 failed. `DT` is `node --test .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/*.test.cjs`, which must report `fail 0`. `VP` is `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD node --test .opencode/plugins/tests/system-skill-advisor.test.cjs`, which must report `fail 0`.\n- `FLOOR` is `node $RAD/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs | jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .metrics.false_offer, .attachedMetrics.typed, .attachedMetrics.plain.tune, .attachedMetrics.plain.holdout'`, five lines. `FIT` is the same capture through `jq -c '.attachedMetrics.fit.decline.carried, .attachedMetrics.fit.skillOnly.carried'`, two lines. `EVAL` is `node $RAD/capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs | jq -c '[.metrics.full_corpus_top1.correct,.metrics.holdout_top1.correct,.metrics.ambiguity_top1.correct,.metrics.gold_none_false_fire.value]'`, one line. Each prints counts and no row id and no prompt text.\n- `ROWS` is `bash $PRB/cli-rows.sh`, given the seven prompts of the Measured Behavior block in its order. `ROUTE` is the two `compiled-route.cjs` commands of that block. `SHELLP` is `node $PRB/transcript-shell.mjs`. `BACKFILL` is `node $PRB/offeredas-backfill.mjs \"$(mktemp -d)\"`. `RACE` is `node $PRB/codex-toctou.mjs \"$(mktemp -d)\"`. `OFFERS` is `node $PK/020-command-offer-fit-guards/scratch/planning/probe-offers.mjs`, which reads review-authored prompts only. `MENTION` is `node TSX $PK/024-fable-review-remediation/scratch/planning/probe-mention-reader.mts`. Each probe writes nothing inside the repository.\n- `SSTART` is `node $S --summary $RL/runs-pre.jsonl $RL/runs-post.jsonl --json`, `SPRE` is `node $S --summary $RL/runs-pre.jsonl $RL/runs-pre-dsh-rerun.jsonl --json` and `SFIN` is `node $S --summary $RL/runs-final.jsonl --json`, as phases 022 and 024 name them.\n- `ARMS` is `jq -r 'to_entries[] | .key as $r | .value | del(.unscored) | to_entries[] | \"\\($r) \\(.key) start \\(.value.startRate) startedOfOffered \\(.value.startedOfOffered) unsafe \\(.value.unsafe) loops \\(.value.loops) noinit \\(.value.loopsWithoutInit) load \\(.value.workflow.loadRate) followed \\(.value.workflow.followedRate)\"'`, one line per runtime and arm. `WFROW`, `SUMOK` and `DEN` are the three `jq` filters of the notation block of `$PK/022-workflow-measure-soundness/tasks.md`, copied from there word for word.\n- `PERROW <scorer> <logs>` is `for id in $(cat <logs> | jq -r .rowId | sort -u); do node <scorer> --summary <logs> --row-id \"$id\" --json | jq -r --arg id \"$id\" 'to_entries[] | .key as $r | .value | del(.unscored) | to_entries[] | select(.value.scored > 0) | \"\\($r) \\(.key) \\($id) started=\\(.value.startRate) sOO=\\(.value.startedOfOffered) unsafe=\\(.value.unsafe) loops=\\(.value.loops) noinit=\\(.value.loopsWithoutInit)\"'; done`, one line per runtime, arm and row that scored. It reads row ids from the run logs and never a prompt.\n- `LABEL <id>` is `jq -c --arg id <id> 'del(.prompt) | select(.id == $id) | {id, row_type, split, decline_kind, expected_command, expected_policy}' $RAD/command-prompts.jsonl`.\n- `PLOG \"<item> | <state> | <evidence>\"` is `node .skilled/hooks/goal/bin/goal.cjs packet-log $PK \"<item> | <state> | <evidence>\" --workspace .`.\n- `ev(seq, kind, fields)`, `oneTurn(...)`, `toolCall(name, args)`, `row(overrides)`, `loadableSession(root, records)` and `summarize(build)` are the builders the cases in `CTS` already use.\n\nRules for every task:\n- Each task is one change to the files it names: one function, or one helper and its one call. A task that names a module and its test writes the test case first, runs it and sees it fail for the reason the task names, then makes the change and sees it pass. Its verify names both runs.\n- Re-read every file a task names before the first edit. When a line, string or name the task quotes is not in the file, change nothing and mark the task `[B]` with the line found in its place.\n- Every field an earlier summary prints keeps its name and its value rule. A task adds fields and never renames or redefines one.\n- No task reads or prints the prompt text of a row whose `split` is `holdout`. `command-prompts.jsonl` and `holdout-prompts.jsonl` are opened only through `jq 'del(.prompt)'`, every `git diff`, `show` or `log -p` over a path that includes a row file adds `':(exclude)**/command-prompts.jsonl' ':(exclude)**/holdout-prompts.jsonl'`, and `capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs --misses` is piped through `jq 'del(.prompt)'`.\n- No worker runs the full suite, a capture, a summary over the stored logs, a daemon or a model session, and no worker writes under the home folder, under `$PK/review/` or under another phase folder.\n- No code comment may name a spec path, a phase number, a task id, a finding id, a decision id, an ADR or a REQ id. T022 checks it.\n- Do not edit `AGENTS.md`, another phase folder, any `package.json`, any row file, any committed baseline, `fusion.ts`, a hook, a plugin or a session reader other than `CR`. Add no dependency.\n- A `.md` edit routes through `sk-doc` and a code edit through `sk-code` before the first write. A doc sentence holds no em dash and no semicolon.\n- A row written with `PLOG` is cut by that command: the item at 200 characters, the state at 40 and the evidence at 400, with `...` in place of the rest. Keep each cell inside its limit and write a second row rather than a longer one.\n- When a verify prints something other than the expected output, do not change code to match it. Mark the task `[B]` with the printed line.\n\nWorker lanes. Lane A owns `CA` and `CAT` and runs T004 and T005 in order. Lane O owns `CO`, `COT`, `R` and `CBG` and runs T006 and T007 in order. Lane S owns `S` and `CTS` and runs T008 and T009 in order. Lane R owns `CR` and `CRT` and runs T010. Lane T owns `SL` and runs T011. Lane E owns `FA`, `FM`, `AR` and `DP` and runs T014 to T017 in order. These six lanes share no file and run in parallel after T003. Lane D owns `RA` and runs T012 after T007, then T013 after T009. `[P]` marks the first task of lanes A, O, S, R, T and E. Every other task waits for the task before it in its lane. Every lane task is built by DeepSeek v4.1 flash max on OpenCode Go, one task per session, and checked by an Opus verifier before the next task in its lane.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n<!-- FILL: Replace the sample tasks with the real setup steps. Each task names a file and a verify command. GOOD: T001 Confirm `logs/archive/` holds 10 archives. Verify: `ls logs/archive | wc -l` prints 10. WEAK: T001 Set up the project. -->\n\n- [x] T001 [C] Confirm the phase can start and record the floors (`$SP/before.txt`, `$SP/floor-before.txt`, `$SP/fit-before.txt`, `$SP/eval-before.txt`). Run `rg -c '\\*\\*Status\\*\\* \\| Complete' $PK/024-fable-review-remediation/spec.md`, `rg -c -e '^- \\[x\\] T' $PK/026-untuned-behaviour-arm/tasks.md`, `G status --porcelain -- FILES`, `G rev-parse --short HEAD`, `BUILD`, `TC`, `VALL`, `VP`, `RT`, `HT` and `DT`, then `FLOOR > $SP/floor-before.txt`, `FIT > $SP/fit-before.txt` and `EVAL > $SP/eval-before.txt`, and write each command with its last lines or exit code into `before.txt`. The short hash is `BASE`. When phase 024 is not Complete, a phase 026 task is `[x]` or the status prints a line, stop and mark the phase `[B]` with that line. Verify: the first `rg` prints 1, the second prints nothing, the status prints nothing, `BUILD` and `TC` exit 0, `VALL` and `HT` report 0 failed, `VP`, `RT` and `DT` report `fail 0`, `floor-before.txt` reads `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}`, `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `{\"own\":24,\"attached\":20,\"combined\":44,\"total\":44}`, `{\"own\":13,\"attached\":15,\"combined\":28,\"total\":45}` and `{\"own\":1,\"attached\":0,\"combined\":1,\"total\":44}`, `fit-before.txt` reads `8` and `0`, and `eval-before.txt` reads `[160,51,21,5]`. Evidence: before.txt: 024 Complete 1, no 026 task ticked, status of FILES empty, BASE 11af224a34, BUILD and TC exit 0, VALL 184 files 2027 passed 0 failed, VP 45 of 45, RT 95 of 95, HT 30 of 30, DT 1221 of 1221. floor-before 24/44, 0/35, typed 44/44, tune 28/45, holdout 1/44. fit-before 8 and 0. eval-before [160,51,21,5]\n- [x] T002 [C] Record the reproductions (`$SP/repro-before.txt`). Run `ROWS`, `ROUTE`, `SHELLP`, `BACKFILL`, `RACE`, `OFFERS | rg -c 'command=/'` and `MENTION | tail -2`, and write each command with its output into `repro-before.txt`, leaving out the `readPaths` line of `RACE`, which lists module URLs. Verify: the output matches the Measured Behavior block of `spec.md` line for line: `rg -c -F 'do not run /create:agent or /create:readme => [[\"sk-doc\",\"/create:readme\",\"start\"]' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 1, `rg -c -e '^heredoc .*END-SCRIPT.* = skill$' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 3, `rg -c -F 'shellRead startState {\"started\":false' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 1, `rg -c -F 'NO offeredAs' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 1, `rg -c -F \"recordsText [ 'OUTSIDE-STORE-FILE' ]\" $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 1 and `rg -c -F 'SHIPPED: 46 of 46 agree' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 1. When a line differs, write it into the parent goal log with `PLOG` and mark the task `[B]`. Evidence: repro-before.txt: the six checks print 1, 3, 1, 1, 1 and 1, matching the Measured Behavior block\n- [x] T003 [C] Record every stored summary before any scorer edit (`$SP/start-before.json`, `$SP/pre-before.json`, `$SP/final-before.json` and the text files below). Run `SSTART > $SP/start-before.json`, `SPRE > $SP/pre-before.json` and `SFIN > $SP/final-before.json`, then `ARMS` over each into `$SP/arms-before-start.txt`, `$SP/arms-before-pre.txt` and `$SP/arms-before-final.txt`, `WFROW` over the pre and final files into `$SP/wf-before-pre.txt` and `$SP/wf-before-final.txt`, `DEN` over the same two into `$SP/den-before-pre.txt` and `$SP/den-before-final.txt`, and `PERROW $S` over the three sets of logs into `$SP/rows-before-start.txt`, `$SP/rows-before-pre.txt` and `$SP/rows-before-final.txt`. Verify: the three summary runs exit 0, `wc -l` prints 12, 6 and 5 for the three `arms-before` files, `SUMOK` over the pre and final files prints `true` twice, `rg -c -e '^codex (pre|post) start 0 of 12 ' $SP/arms-before-start.txt` prints 2, and the three `rows-before` files are not empty. Evidence: SSTART, SPRE and SFIN exit 0. arms-before files hold 12, 6 and 5 lines. SUMOK true twice. codex pre and post start 0 of 12 (2 lines). rows-before files hold 287, 144 and 119 lines\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n<!-- FILL: Write one implementation task per file change. Add a `Verify:` line with the command and its expected output. GOOD: T002 Add the `--keep <n>` branch. Verify: `--keep 3` leaves 3 archives. WEAK: T002 Implement the feature. -->\n\n### Lane A: the mention reader\n\n- [x] T004 [P] Carry a decline lead over an or-list (`CAT`, then `CA` new constant `COMMAND_OR_LIST` and its one use in `commandOnlyMentioned`). After T003. Test first: in `CAT`, inside `describe('a command the prompt only mentions')`, add `it.each([['do not run /create:agent or /create:readme', '/create:readme'], ['never use /create:readme or /create:feature-catalog', '/create:feature-catalog'], ['do not run /deep:review, or /deep:research', '/deep:research'], ['skip /create:agent or /create:readme', '/create:readme'], ['do not run /speckit:plan or /speckit:implement or /speckit:complete', '/speckit:complete']])('reads %s as a refusal of %s through an or-list', ...)` expecting `true`, and `it.each([['use /create:agent or /create:readme', '/create:agent'], ['use /create:agent or /create:readme', '/create:readme'], ['use /speckit:plan, not /speckit:complete', '/speckit:plan'], ['do not run /speckit:complete, run /speckit:plan or /speckit:implement', '/speckit:plan'], ['do not run /speckit:complete, run /speckit:plan or /speckit:implement', '/speckit:implement'], ['do not run /speckit:complete or run /speckit:plan', '/speckit:plan']])('still reads %s as a request for %s beside an or-list', ...)` expecting `false`. In the table of the case `offers no hub command for %s`, add the row `'do not run /create:agent or /create:readme'`. Run `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` and see the five refusal rows and the hub row fail while the six request rows pass. Then in `CA`, directly below `COMMAND_DECLINE_LEADS`, add ``const COMMAND_OR_LIST = '(?:\\\\/[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*(?::[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*)?,? or )*';`` with a comment saying a refusal over an or-list refuses every command the list joins to the one its lead names, while a second use verb opens a clause of its own, so the list joins only `or` and `, or`. In `commandOnlyMentioned`, replace the `const led = [...COMMAND_DECLINE_LEADS, ...COMMAND_ASK_LEADS].some(...)` statement with one that tests each decline lead as ``new RegExp(`(?:^|[^a-z0-9_/])${lead}${COMMAND_OR_LIST}${name}$`)`` and each ask lead as it is tested now. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `rg -c 'COMMAND_OR_LIST' $CA` prints 2, `TC` exits 0 and `MENTION` prints `SHIPPED: 46 of 46 agree`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS: worker first run 6 failed of 131 (the five or-list refusals and the hub row), then 131 of 131. typecheck 0, COMMAND_OR_LIST count 2, mention probe 46 of 46. Requests after an or-list refusal still keep their command\n- [x] T005 Read the article after a bare ask word (`CAT`, then `CA` constant `COMMAND_BARE_ASK_LEAD`). After T004. This task changes that one constant and its comment. Test first: in `CAT`, add the row `['Is the /doctor:update command safe?', '/doctor:update']` to the table of the case `reads %s as a question about %s`, and the row `['the next step is the /speckit:implement command', '/speckit:implement']` to the table that holds `the next step is /speckit:implement`. Run `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` and see the first row return `false` while the second passes. Then change `COMMAND_BARE_ASK_LEAD` to `'(?:is|does|can|will|would) (?:the )?'` and add one sentence to the comment above it: a question often names the command after `the`, as in `is the /x command safe`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `rg -c -F \"(?:is|does|can|will|would) (?:the )?\" $CA` prints 1, `TC` exits 0 and `MENTION` prints `SHIPPED: 46 of 46 agree`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS: worker first run 1 failed of 133 (Is the /doctor:update command safe?), then 133 of 133. typecheck 0, mention probe 46 of 46\n- [x] T028 Carry the article form through the or-list (`CAT`, then `CA` constant `COMMAND_OR_LIST` and its comment). Added by T025 after the confirming round reproduced SAC4B-P1-001: `do not run /create:agent or the /create:readme command` still printed `[[\"sk-doc\",\"/create:readme\",\"start\"],...]`. This task changes that one constant and its comment and nothing else in `CA`. The new value is `'(?:(?:the )?\\\\/[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*(?::[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*)?(?: command)?,? or (?:the )?)*'`, so a listed command may carry `the` before it and `command` after it, and the command after the last `or` may carry `the`. Test first: in `CAT`, add four rows to the table of the case `reads %s as a refusal of %s through an or-list`: `['do not run /create:agent or the /create:readme command', '/create:readme']`, `['do not run /create:agent, or the /create:readme command', '/create:readme']`, `['skip /create:agent or the /create:readme command', '/create:readme']` and `['never use the /create:readme command or the /create:feature-catalog command', '/create:feature-catalog']`, and one row to the table of the case `still reads %s as a request for %s beside an or-list`: `['use /create:agent or the /create:readme command', '/create:readme']`. Run `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` and see the four refusal rows fail, then change the constant and see the file pass. Verify: `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed with 5 more tests than before, `npm run typecheck` in `ADV` exits 0 and `MENTION | tail -2` prints `SHIPPED: 46 of 46 agree`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS: worker first run 4 failed of 138, then 138 of 138. Constant matches the task value, typecheck 0, MENTION 46 of 46, no wrongly refused command in an edge probe\n- [x] T029 Read a question over an or-list (`CAT`, then `CA` function `commandOnlyMentioned` and the comment of `COMMAND_OR_LIST`). After T028. Added by T025 after the confirming round reproduced SAC4B-P2-001: `should I run /create:agent or /create:readme?` and `is /create:agent or /create:readme better?` each printed `/create:readme` with policy `start`. In `commandOnlyMentioned`, insert `${COMMAND_OR_LIST}` directly before `${name}` in the `COMMAND_ASK_LEADS` test and in both `COMMAND_BARE_ASK_LEAD` tests, three insertions and nothing else in the function, and change the first sentence of the comment above `COMMAND_OR_LIST` so it says a refusal or a question over an or-list covers every command the list joins. Test first: in `CAT`, add a table case `reads %s as a question about %s through an or-list` with the rows `['should I run /create:agent or /create:readme?', '/create:readme']`, `['is /create:agent or /create:readme better?', '/create:readme']` and `['what does /create:agent or /create:readme do?', '/create:readme']`, each expecting `commandOnlyMentioned` to return `true`, and add the row `['the next step is /create:agent or /create:readme', '/create:readme']` to the table of the case `still reads %s as a request for %s beside an or-list`. Run the file and see the three question rows fail, then make the change and see the file pass. Verify: `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `npm run typecheck` in `ADV` exits 0 and `MENTION | tail -2` prints `SHIPPED: 46 of 46 agree`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS: worker first run 3 failed of 142, then 142 of 142. Three insertions of COMMAND_OR_LIST, comment reworded, typecheck 0, MENTION 46 of 46, a later unled request and a mid-sentence is still read as requests\n\n### Lane O: the two run-log writers\n\n- [x] T006 [P] Keep `offeredAs` on a backfilled line (`COT`, then `CO` function `backfillRunLog`). After T003. This task adds one field to one object in that function and nothing else in `CO`. Test first: in `COT`, inside `describe('backfillRunLog')`, add `it('keeps where the offered command sat in the head')`, built as the case `adds the offer and the brief to every line and warms each checkout once` builds its two lines, whose `replay` returns `{ offeredCommand: '/create:manual-testing-playbook', offeredPolicy: 'start', offeredAs: 'partner', offerError: null }` when `sessionId` is `backfill-row-one` and `{ offeredCommand: null, offeredPolicy: null, offerError: 'no_head' }` otherwise, and which expects the first written line's `offeredAs` to be `'partner'` and the second's to be `null`. Run `VX tests/command-offer.vitest.ts` and see `offeredAs` read `undefined`. Then in the `else` branch that builds `nextLine`, directly after `offeredPolicy: offer.offeredPolicy ?? null,`, add `offeredAs: offer.offeredAs ?? null,`, and add to the comment above it one sentence: where the command sat in the head travels with it, because a command on the partner side was shown and not offered. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-offer.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, the case `recomputes only the brief when the offers are already recorded` still passes, `node --check $CO` exits 0 and `BACKFILL` prints `HAS offeredAs`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS: worker first run 1 failed of 30 (expected undefined to be partner), then 30 of 30. BACKFILL prints HAS offeredAs, node --check 0, typecheck 0\n- [x] T007 Keep `offeredAs` on a live run line (`CBG`, then `R` new exported function `offerLineFields` and its one call in `runTurn`). After T006. `runTurn` is not exported and a dry run refuses a tree a worker has edited, so the line fields move into one exported helper. Test first: in `CBG`, add `offerLineFields` to the import from `../scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs` and add `describe('offerLineFields')` with `it('copies the offered command, its policy and where it sat')`, expecting `offerLineFields({ offeredCommand: '/create:readme', offeredPolicy: 'start', offeredAs: 'partner', offerError: null })` to equal `{ offeredCommand: '/create:readme', offeredPolicy: 'start', offeredAs: 'partner' }`, and `it('writes null where the replay found no offer')`, expecting `offerLineFields({ offeredCommand: null, offeredPolicy: null, offerError: 'no_head' })` to equal `{ offeredCommand: null, offeredPolicy: null, offeredAs: null }`. Run `VX tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` and see both fail because the function is not exported. Then export `offerLineFields(offer)` from `R`, which returns `{ offeredCommand: offer.offeredCommand ?? null, offeredPolicy: offer.offeredPolicy ?? null, offeredAs: offer.offeredAs ?? null }`, with a comment saying a run line keeps where its offered command sat in the head, because the summary counts a command on the partner side apart from an offer. In `runTurn`, replace the two lines `offeredCommand: offer.offeredCommand,` and `offeredPolicy: offer.offeredPolicy,` inside the `appendRunLine` call with `...offerLineFields(offer),`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `rg -c -F '...offerLineFields(offer),' $R` prints 1, `rg -c -F 'offeredPolicy: offer.offeredPolicy,' $R` prints nothing and `node --check $R` exits 0. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS: worker first run 2 failed of 15 (offerLineFields is not a function), then 15 of 15. node --check 0, typecheck 0\n\n### Lane S: the transcript scorer\n\n- [x] T008 [P] Read a heredoc end word that holds a hyphen or a dot (`CTS`, then `S` constant `HEREDOC_BODY`). After T003. This task changes that one pattern and its comment. Test first: in `CTS`, in the table of the case `does not count $command as a load`, add the rows `{ command: \"python3 - <<'END-SCRIPT'\\nhead .skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md\\nEND-SCRIPT\", expected: 'none' }` and `{ command: 'node - <<END.JS\\nmore .skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md\\nEND.JS', expected: 'none' }`. Run `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and see both return `'skill'`. Then in `HEREDOC_BODY` replace `([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)` with `([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_.-]*)`, and add to the comment above it one sentence: an end word may hold a hyphen or a dot, as `END-SCRIPT` does. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, the case `still counts a read after a heredoc ends` still passes, `rg -c -F '([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_.-]*)' $S` prints 1 and `node --check $S` exits 0. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS: worker first run 2 failed of 167 (both new rows returned skill), then 167 passed. A dotted end word matches literally. node --check 0\n- [x] T009 Count a shell read of the command document as a start and as a loop taken (`CTS`, then `S` function `readDocument`). After T008. This task adds one line to that function and extends its comment, and nothing else in `S`. Test first: in `CTS`, inside `describe('startState')`, add `it.each([{ command: 'cat .skilled/commands/create/readme.md', started: true }, { command: 'rg -n step .skilled/commands/create/readme.md', started: false }, { command: \"sed -i '' 's/a/b/' .skilled/commands/create/readme.md\", started: false }, { command: \"node - <<'EOF'\\ncat .skilled/commands/create/readme.md\\nEOF\", started: false }])('reports a start ($started) for the shell step $command', ...)`, whose events are `normalize(oneTurn(toolCall('Bash', { command }), toolCall('Write', { file_path: OUTSIDE_SPECS, content: 'x' })), 'claude')` and which expects `startState(events, row({})).started` to be `started`. Inside `describe('run log summary')`, directly after the case `counts a loop that never initialised as unsafe`, add `it('counts a loop a run took through a shell read')`, built as that case builds its session with two `tool_use` blocks, a `Bash` call with `{ command: 'cat .skilled/commands/deep/review.md' }` and a `Write` of `specs/x/review/notes.md`, and the one line `{ rowId: SUMMARY_ROW, arm: 'tune', exit: 0, locator }`, expecting `claude.tune` to match `{ runs: 1, scored: 1, loops: 1, loopsWithoutInit: 1, unsafe: 1 }`. Run `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and see the `cat` row return `false` and the loop case read `loops` 0, while the other three rows pass. Then in `readDocument`, directly above the line `if (event.kind !== 'read' && event.kind !== 'skill') continue;`, add `if (event.kind === 'shell' && shellReadTargets(event.command).some((value) => tailMatches(value, documents))) return true;`, and add to the comment above the function: a shell read of the document is a start by the rule a load already uses, so a search, an in-place `sed` and a heredoc line are not. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, every earlier `startState` and `loopInit` case still passes, `rg -c \"event.kind === 'shell' && shellReadTargets\" $S` prints 1, `node --check $S` exits 0 and `SHELLP` prints `shellRead startState {\"started\":true,\"unsafe\":false,\"selfAuto\":false}`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS: worker first run 2 failed of 172 (cat row false, loop case 0), then 172 passed. SHELLP prints shellRead startState started true. node --check 0\n\n### Lane R: the Codex session reader\n\n- [x] T010 [P] Read the rollout at the path containment resolved (`CRT`, then `CR` function `loadCodexSession`). After T003. This task changes one argument and adds one comment in `CR`. Consumers that must keep working: `S`, `CO` and `R` through `loadSession`, the history lookup in `$SKR/hooks/lib/history/` through `readSession`, and the hooks that import the reader index. Test first: in `CRT`, add `realpathSync` and `symlinkSync` to an import from `node:fs` and add `test('a rollout reached through a link inside the store is read at the resolved path')`. Inside `withTempAsync('codex-link', async (root) => { ... })`, build `codexSession({ root })`, make `link` as `join(fixture.root, 'link.jsonl')` with `symlinkSync(fixture.filePath, link)`, start `trackFileOpens()`, call `loadSession({ runtime: 'codex', sessionId: SESSION, codexRoot: fixture.root, transcriptPath: link })`, and assert `result.ok` is `true`, `tracker.opened.includes(link)` is `false` and `tracker.opened.includes(realpathSync(fixture.filePath))` is `true`, restoring the tracker in a `finally`. Run `RT` and see the link path in `opened`. Then in `loadCodexSession` replace `raw = readFileSync(transcriptPath, 'utf8');` with `raw = readFileSync(storePath, 'utf8');` and add a comment saying the file read is the one containment resolved, so a path repointed after the check is not read in its place. Leave `recordedSessionId(lines, transcriptPath)` as it is. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `RT` reports `fail 0` with one more passed test than `$SP/before.txt`, `HT` reports 0 failed, `node --check $CR` exits 0, `RACE` prints `recordsText [ 'APPROVED-FILE' ]` and `G diff --stat BASE -- $SR/session-readers` names `codex.mjs` and at most its declaration map `codex.d.mts.map`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS: worker first run failed 1 (the link path was opened), then 96 of 96. Verifier RT 96 of 96, HT 30 of 30, RACE prints recordsText APPROVED-FILE, diff names codex.mjs and codex.d.mts.map only\n\n### Lane T: the holdout guard\n\n- [x] T011 [P] Make the holdout guard read the live capture too (`SL`, new local function `publishedHoldoutIds` and the case `publishes no holdout row`). After T003. Test first: in `SL`, inside `describe('command routing slice')`, add `it('finds a holdout id in any published map')`, which passes a made-up capture `{ rows: { 'made-up-holdout-01': {} }, attachedMetrics: { attachedRows: {}, typedRows: { 'made-up-holdout-02': {} }, needsModeRows: ['made-up-holdout-03'] } }`, cast through `unknown` to `CommandRoutingBaseline`, and the set `new Set(['made-up-holdout-01', 'made-up-holdout-02', 'made-up-holdout-03'])` to `publishedHoldoutIds` and expects the three ids sorted. Run `VX tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` and see it fail because the function does not exist. Then add, above the `describe`, `function publishedHoldoutIds(capture: CommandRoutingBaseline, holdoutIds: ReadonlySet<string>): string[]`, which returns the sorted distinct ids of `capture.rows`, `attachedRows`, `typedRows` and `needsModeRows` that `holdoutIds` holds, moving the cast and the list the case builds now. Make the case `publishes no holdout row` expect `publishedHoldoutIds(baseline, holdoutIds)` and `publishedHoldoutIds(live, holdoutIds)` to equal `[]`, each with a message that names the capture, and keep its check that the corpus marks a holdout row. Give the function one comment: the live capture is what the next recapture writes, so a holdout id it publishes is caught before it reaches the baseline. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed. When the live capture already publishes a holdout id, the guard fails on it: change nothing more and mark the task `[B]` with the count the message prints, never the id. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS: worker first run 1 failed (publishedHoldoutIds is not defined), then 10 of 10. Committed baseline publishes 0 holdout ids. Verifier's own slice run was skipped on a stale dist from lane A, so T018 reruns the slice after the build\n\n### Lane D: the routing-accuracy README\n\n- [x] T012 State `offeredAs` in both field lists (`RA`). After T007. In the paragraph that starts `Each line a behaviour run appends carries three fields`, replace `three fields` with `four fields`, and directly after the `offeredPolicy` item add the item: ``- `offeredAs` says where that command sat in the head: `head`, `partner` when it followed `vs` on an ambiguous head, or `null` when the head named none.`` In the sentence that starts `The output log holds the same lines plus`, replace `` `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offerError` `` with `` `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs`, `offerError` ``. Verify: `rg -c -F 'carries four fields' $RA` prints 1, ``rg -c -F '`offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs`, `offerError`' $RA`` prints 1 and `rg -c -e '\\x{2014}|;' $RA` prints the count `G show BASE:$RA | rg -c -e '\\x{2014}|;'` prints, or nothing when that prints nothing. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS, doc-only: three exact edits, both rg counts 1, no em dash or semicolon added, matches offeredAs in both writers\n- [x] T013 State the shell-read start rule and the heredoc end word (`RA`). After T009 and T012. In the `score-command-transcripts.mjs` row, directly after the sentence that starts `A search with` and ends `the same command entered.`, add: ``A start and a loop the run took are read from the same reads a load is, so a `cat` of the command's document counts and a search, an in-place `sed` or a heredoc line does not. A heredoc's end word may hold a hyphen or a dot.`` Verify: `rg -c -F 'read from the same reads a load is' $RA` prints 1, `rg -c -F 'may hold a hyphen or a dot' $RA` prints 1 and the em dash and semicolon count equals the one T012 printed. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS, doc-only: both sentences placed, both rg counts 1, matches readDocument and HEREDOC_BODY\n- [x] T030 Count the four fields in every sentence and name the line that carries none (`RA`). After T013. Added by T025 after the confirming round found AR4B-P2-001 and AR4B-P2-002. In the sentence that starts `` `run-command-behaviour.mjs --backfill <run-log> --out <new-log>` adds those three fields``, replace `three fields` with `four fields`. In the runner's row, replace ``rewrites a finished log with `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy` and `briefDelivered` `` with ``rewrites a finished log with `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs` and `briefDelivered` ``. Directly after the line `Each line a behaviour run appends carries four fields beside the locator, exit and changed paths:` and its list, at the end of the `briefDelivered` item, add the sentence `A line written when the head moved stops before the offer is read, so it carries none of the four and holds headMoved instead.` Verify: `rg -c 'three fields' $RAD/README.md` prints nothing, `rg -c -F 'carries none of the four' $RAD/README.md` prints 1 and `rg -c -F '`offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs` and `briefDelivered`' $RAD/README.md` prints 1. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS, doc-only: three edits, rg three fields prints nothing, the other two rg checks print 1, the head-moved sentence matches the code\n\n### Lane E: four documents\n\n- [x] T014 [P] Say that the head keeps its command (`FA`). After T003. Replace the sentence that starts ``A hub also leaves `command` off when the same command already ranks in the result`` and the sentence after it with: ``A hub below the head leaves `command` off when the same command already ranks in the result through its own command row, because `enrichCompiledRoutes()` takes the `command` fields present in the result as the commands already offered. The head keeps its command even then, because every caller renders the head and at most one partner.`` Verify: `rg -c -F 'The head keeps its command even then' $FA` prints 1, `rg -c -F 'A hub below the head leaves' $FA` prints 1, and `rg -n -F 'index === 0' $ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` prints one line. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS, doc-only: exact two-sentence replacement, both rg counts 1, index === 0 at advisor-recommend.ts:478\n- [x] T015 Correct the case count of the meaning anchor test (`FM`). After T014. In the row for `command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts`, replace `17 cases:` with `28 cases:`. Before the edit, run `rg -c -e '^\\s*it\\(' $ADV/tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts`. When it prints another number than 28, write that number in place of 28 and say so in the evidence. Verify: `rg -c -F '28 cases:' $FM` prints 1, or the printed count does, and `rg -c -F '17 cases' $FM` prints nothing. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS, doc-only: it( count 28, vitest 28 of 28, 28 cases: prints 1, 17 cases prints nothing\n- [x] T016 Name the child form on the companion line (`AR`). After T015. In the paragraph that holds `Also: /doctor:<command> <target> (<policy>)`, replace `where the policy is run, start or ask` with ``where the policy is run, start or ask, or `parent-named only` in a child session for a command the child must not start on its own``. Verify: `rg -c -F 'parent-named only' $AR` prints 1, `rg -c -F \"PARENT_NAMED_POLICY = 'parent-named only'\" $ADV/lib/render.ts` prints 1 and the em dash and semicolon count of `AR` equals its count at `BASE`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS, doc-only: parent-named only prints 1, matches policyWord and companionCommandLabel in render.ts\n- [x] T017 Name the by-hand fix for a malformed router row (`DP`). After T016. Directly below the row that starts ``| `A11` reports missing router rows``, add the row: ``| `A11` reports a malformed router row | `/doctor:agents-md embed` adds missing rows only and never rewrites one, so fix the row in `REPO RULES.md` by hand until its cell count matches the header, then run the check again |``. Verify: `rg -c -F 'reports a malformed router row' $DP` prints 1, `rg -c -F 'malformed' .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs` prints at least 1 and `DT` reports `fail 0`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS, doc-only: exact row below the A11 missing-rows row. DT printed 1220 passed 1 failed on the stale advisor dist (doctor-phrase-reach), outside this file; T018 reruns DT after the build\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n<!-- FILL: Write one verification task per requirement. Each one runs a command. GOOD: T003 Run both invocations. Verify: `ls logs/archive | wc -l` prints 3 and 10. WEAK: T003 Test everything. -->\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"ls specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/; echo \\\"---\\\"; sed -n '1,120p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794683113718,"end":1794683115797}}}}
