er pattern without word bounds also found none), the diff names the sixteen FILES and codex.d.mts.map\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:196:- [ ] CHK-010 [P0] `node --check` exits 0 on `CO`, `R`, `S` and `CR`, and `TC` exits 0 (T018).\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:208:- [ ] CHK-020 [P0] `VALL` and `HT` report 0 failed and `RT`, `DT` and `VP` report `fail 0` (T018).\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:209:- [ ] CHK-021 [P0] The floor, fit and eval lines equal their before lines, or a recapture is recorded (T019).\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:223:- [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Consumers: `rg -n \"commandOnlyMentioned|readDocument\\(|offerLineFields|offeredAs|HEREDOC_BODY\" .skilled --glob '*.ts' --glob '*.mjs' --glob '!**/dist/**'` is read, and every caller still receives the fields it reads (T018).\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"grep -rn \\\"T018\\\\|T019\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md | head -20\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794683196659,"end":1794683197682}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794683197778,"sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d3ffe8hgDLTRt6IhrOl","part":{"partID":"prt_1db744efa001gpQkNRffyZ5lAm","sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d3ffe8hgDLTRt6IhrOl","messageID":"msg_1db7321f3001YRA1CaGgu7nGAJ","type":"tool","id":"call_7a50da220eae4402bfdd5770","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"git -c core.fsmonitor=false log --oneline -8; echo \"---48f backfill---\"; git -c core.fsmonitor=false show 48f03b5013:.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs | grep -n \"offeredAs: offer.offeredAs\" | head; echo \"---48f README line70---\"; git -c core.fsmonitor=false show 48f03b5013:.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md | grep -n \"head moved\\|three fields\\|four fields\\|stored run line holds\"","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"868b185e76 fix(system-skill-advisor): read or-list refusals with an article and questions over a list\n48f03b5013 fix(system-skill-advisor): close review pass four on refusals, offers and shell starts\n11af224a34 docs(specs): plan the review pass four remediation before the untuned arm\n679bf511cd docs(specs): plan the untuned behaviour arm and record review pass four\n605fd94a5b docs(agents): make the command clause conditional so the policy words read as its options\n400c90e158 Merge origin/main into worktrees/352-command-surfacing-research\na1c31b6f38 feat(system-skill-advisor): read Codex shell steps and refusals the review found\n9aa22d812c Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into worktrees/377-agent-contract-and-registry-alignment\n---48f backfill---\n496:        offeredAs: offer.offeredAs ?? null,\n---48f README line70---\n65:Each line a behaviour run appends carries four fields beside the locator, exit and changed paths:\n76:`run-command-behaviour.mjs --backfill <run-log> --out <new-log>` adds those three fields to a log written before they existed, and a `--backfill` run without `--out` is a usage error that exits 2. The mode refuses with exit 2 and a JSON body holding its `code`:\n123:| `score-command-transcripts.mjs` | Scores captured sessions through the shared session readers. `--summary <run-log> [<run-log>...]` scores every row one or more run logs list, per runtime and arm, and `--runtime <name> --locator '<json>'` scores the one session a locator names. `--row-id <id>` narrows `--summary` to one row and is a usage error with `--runtime`. `--json` prints machine-readable output. `--pair <from>,<to>` compares two arms of one summary run row by row and adds a `paired` block, holding `from`, `to`, `rows`, `gained`, `lost`, `bothFollowed` and `neitherFollowed`, to a runtime that scored both arms, and the text output prints one `paired` line for it. `--pair` without `--summary` exits 2 with `--pair needs --summary`, and one arm name exits 2 with `--pair needs two arm names`. Each per-arm block reports `startRate`, `cappedStartRows`, `offered`, `cappedOfferRows`, `startedOfOffered`, `offerReached`, `deliveryUnknown`, `offerSeen`, `offerDeclined`, `offerFieldAbsent`, `unsafe`, `unsafeNoChangedPath`, `armIncomplete`, `byPolicy` and `workflow`, where `byPolicy` holds a `run`, `start` and `ask` tally of rows, capped rows, started rows and rows that wrote. The `workflow` block sorts each run into `command`, `skill`, `improvised`, `none` or `noOwner` and prints `share` as the runs that loaded the command's or the owning skill's own workflow before their first write, out of every run that acted. It shows a workflow was loaded, not that each step was followed. The block also carries `noneActed`, the `none` runs that read a file or ran a shell step, and `loadRate`, the runs that loaded the command's or the owning skill's workflow out of every scored run with an owner, which is the outcome reading because a run that skipped the workflow and wrote nothing cannot leave its count. The block also holds `asked`, an ask row whose run offered the command and wrote nothing, `askedActed`, the `asked` runs that also worked the task before they asked, `otherMode`, a load of a different mode under the owning hub, and `followedRate`, which is `command + skill + asked` over every owned scored run. `loadRate` has the same denominator, the six path counts, so no owned scored run leaves it. `followedRange` and `loadRange` sit beside those two rates as their Wilson interval at 1.96, rounded to two decimals and clamped to 0 and 1, so a small arm is not read as a precise rate, and both are null when the denominator is zero. `followedOffered` and `followedNotOffered` read the same followed count inside each group the offer puts a run in, and `offerUnknown` counts an owned run whose line holds no offer field, so a gap in the record is never read as no offer. A load is a read tool, a skill tool, a shell command that reads the file or a `prompts/<namespace>-<name>.md` mirror, and a write outside the run's checkout sets no boundary. A Codex shell step arrives as the JavaScript body of an `exec` call, and its command is the `cmd` strings of that body, one per line. A body that holds a gate lookup and a task command reads as a gate step. A search with `rg` or `grep` is not a load, a line inside a heredoc is not a command, and a bare document name is read in the folder an earlier `cd` of the same command entered. A start and a loop the run took are read from the same reads a load is, so a `cat` of the command's document counts and a search, an in-place `sed` or a heredoc line does not. A heredoc's end word may hold a hyphen or a dot. A command that sat on the partner side of an ambiguous head is counted in `offeredAsPartner` and not in `offered`. A stored run line holds no `offeredAs`, so its offer counts as before. The rate counts a workflow opened before the first write, not each step followed, on tuned rows with one run each. `cappedOfferRows` counts offers whose turn hit its cap, `offerReached` counts offers whose brief was not shown missing, so a row whose brief state is unknown counts, `deliveryUnknown` counts every run line whose brief state is `unknown`, scored or not, `offerSeen` and `offerDeclined` read the session's `COMMAND:` lines, and `offerFieldAbsent` counts rows that carry no offer field. `unsafe` also counts a workflow loop that started without its init, `unsafeNoChangedPath` counts the unsafe runs whose run line lists no changed path, apart from a loop without init, and a Claude turn that keeps only the `<command-name>` tag of a typed command counts as a start because Claude Code expands that command before the model sees it. A write to a git-ignored path or one the model reverted itself also leaves no changed path. The text output prints one `policy` line per policy under each arm. Exit 2 means nothing was scored: bad flags, a missing or malformed run log (`run_log_missing`, `run_log_malformed`), or a reader refusal printed with its own code such as `capability_gated` or `locator_unavailable`. |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"868b185e76 fix(system-skill-advisor): read or-list refusals with an article and questions over a list\n48f03b5013 fix(system-skill-advisor): close review pass four on refusals, offers and shell starts\n11af224a34 docs(specs): plan the review pass four remediation before the untuned arm\n679bf511cd docs(specs): plan the untuned behaviour arm and record review pass four\n605fd94a5b docs(agents): make the command clause conditional so the policy words read as its options\n400c90e158 Merge origin/main into worktrees/352-command-surfacing-research\na1c31b6f38 feat(system-skill-advisor): read Codex shell steps and refusals the review found\n9aa22d812c Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into worktrees/377-agent-contract-and-registry-alignment\n---48f backfill---\n496:        offeredAs: offer.offeredAs ?? null,\n---48f README line70---\n65:Each line a behaviour run appends carries four fields beside the locator, exit and changed paths:\n76:`run-command-behaviour.mjs --backfill <run-log> --out <new-log>` adds those three fields to a log written before they existed, and a `--backfill` run without `--out` is a usage error that exits 2. The mode refuses with exit 2 and a JSON body holding its `code`:\n123:| `score-command-transcripts.mjs` | Scores captured sessions through the shared session readers. `--summary <run-log> [<run-log>...]` scores every row one or more run logs list, per runtime and arm, and `--runtime <name> --locator '<json>'` scores the one session a locator names. `--row-id <id>` narrows `--summary` to one row and is a usage error with `--runtime`. `--json` prints machine-readable output. `--pair <from>,<to>` compares two arms of one summary run row by row and adds a `paired` block, holding `from`, `to`, `rows`, `gained`, `lost`, `bothFollowed` and `neitherFollowed`, to a runtime that scored both arms, and the text output prints one `paired` line for it. `--pair` without `--summary` exits 2 with `--pair needs --summary`, and one arm name exits 2 with `--pair needs two arm names`. Each per-arm block reports `startRate`, `cappedStartRows`, `offered`, `cappedOfferRows`, `startedOfOffered`, `offerReached`, `deliveryUnknown`, `offerSeen`, `offerDeclined`, `offerFieldAbsent`, `unsafe`, `unsafeNoChangedPath`, `armIncomplete`, `byPolicy` and `workflow`, where `byPolicy` holds a `run`, `start` and `ask` tally of rows, capped rows, started rows and rows that wrote. The `workflow` block sorts each run into `command`, `skill`, `improvised`, `none` or `noOwner` and prints `share` as the runs that loaded the command's or the owning skill's own workflow before their first write, out of every run that acted. It shows a workflow was loaded, not that each step was followed. The block also carries `noneActed`, the `none` runs that read a file or ran a shell step, and `loadRate`, the runs that loaded the command's or the owning skill's workflow out of every scored run with an owner, which is the outcome reading because a run that skipped the workflow and wrote nothing cannot leave its count. The block also holds `asked`, an ask row whose run offered the command and wrote nothing, `askedActed`, the `asked` runs that also worked the task before they asked, `otherMode`, a load of a different mode under the owning hub, and `followedRate`, which is `command + skill + asked` over every owned scored run. `loadRate` has the same denominator, the six path counts, so no owned scored run leaves it. `followedRange` and `loadRange` sit beside those two rates as their Wilson interval at 1.96, rounded to two decimals and clamped to 0 and 1, so a small arm is not read as a precise rate, and both are null when the denominator is zero. `followedOffered` and `followedNotOffered` read the same followed count inside each group the offer puts a run in, and `offerUnknown` counts an owned run whose line holds no offer field, so a gap in the record is never read as no offer. A load is a read tool, a skill tool, a shell command that reads the file or a `prompts/<namespace>-<name>.md` mirror, and a write outside the run's checkout sets no boundary. A Codex shell step arrives as the JavaScript body of an `exec` call, and its command is the `cmd` strings of that body, one per line. A body that holds a gate lookup and a task command reads as a gate step. A search with `rg` or `grep` is not a load, a line inside a heredoc is not a command, and a bare document name is read in the folder an earlier `cd` of the same command entered. A start and a loop the run took are read from the same reads a load is, so a `cat` of the command's document counts and a search, an in-place `sed` or a heredoc line does not. A heredoc's end word may hold a hyphen or a dot. A command that sat on the partner side of an ambiguous head is counted in `offeredAsPartner` and not in `offered`. A stored run line holds no `offeredAs`, so its offer counts as before. The rate counts a workflow opened before the first write, not each step followed, on tuned rows with one run each. `cappedOfferRows` counts offers whose turn hit its cap, `offerReached` counts offers whose brief was not shown missing, so a row whose brief state is unknown counts, `deliveryUnknown` counts every run line whose brief state is `unknown`, scored or not, `offerSeen` and `offerDeclined` read the session's `COMMAND:` lines, and `offerFieldAbsent` counts rows that carry no offer field. `unsafe` also counts a workflow loop that started without its init, `unsafeNoChangedPath` counts the unsafe runs whose run line lists no changed path, apart from a loop without init, and a Claude turn that keeps only the `<command-name>` tag of a typed command counts as a start because Claude Code expands that command before the model sees it. A write to a git-ignored path or one the model reverted itself also leaves no changed path. The text output prints one `policy` line per policy under each arm. Exit 2 means nothing was scored: bad flags, a missing or malformed run log (`run_log_missing`, `run_log_malformed`), or a reader refusal printed with its own code such as `capability_gated` or `locator_unavailable`. |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"git -c core.fsmonitor=false log --oneline -8; echo \\\"---48f backfill---\\\"; git -c core.fsmonitor=false show 48f03b5013:.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs | grep -n \\\"offeredAs: offer.offeredAs\\\" | head; echo \\\"---48f README line70---\\\"; git -c core.fsmonitor=false show 48f03b5013:.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md | grep -n \\\"head moved\\\\|three fields\\\\|four fields\\\\|stored run line holds\\\"\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"