{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794683227065,"sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d3ffe8hgDLTRt6IhrOl","part":{"partID":"prt_1db74c3b20020EOX4x7LU4oB1L","sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d3ffe8hgDLTRt6IhrOl","messageID":"msg_1db746ace001pt04for4PcP1Yh","type":"tool","id":"call_0d890550b5774730bb81d950","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"briefOnly\\|brief-only\\|--backfill\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs | head -40; echo \"---\"; sed -n '2000,2060p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"46://   node run-command-behaviour.mjs --backfill <run-log> --out <new-log> [--brief-only]\n982:  `       ${SCRIPT_NAME} --backfill <run-log> --out <new-log> [--brief-only]`,\n1030:    briefOnly: false,\n1059:    } else if (token === '--backfill') {\n1061:      options.backfill = resolve(valueAfter(argv, index, '--backfill'));\n1067:    } else if (token === '--brief-only') {\n1068:      options.briefOnly = true;\n1081:  if (options.briefOnly && options.backfill === null) {\n1082:    throw new UsageError('--brief-only needs --backfill');\n1266:    briefOnly: options.briefOnly,\n---\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"46://   node run-command-behaviour.mjs --backfill <run-log> --out <new-log> [--brief-only]\n982:  `       ${SCRIPT_NAME} --backfill <run-log> --out <new-log> [--brief-only]`,\n1030:    briefOnly: false,\n1059:    } else if (token === '--backfill') {\n1061:      options.backfill = resolve(valueAfter(argv, index, '--backfill'));\n1067:    } else if (token === '--brief-only') {\n1068:      options.briefOnly = true;\n1081:  if (options.briefOnly && options.backfill === null) {\n1082:    throw new UsageError('--brief-only needs --backfill');\n1266:    briefOnly: options.briefOnly,\n---\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"briefOnly\\\\|brief-only\\\\|--backfill\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs | head -40; echo \\\"---\\\"; sed -n '2000,2060p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794683225010,"end":1794683227065}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794683227077,"sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d3ffe8hgDLTRt6IhrOl","part":{"partID":"prt_1db74c7a4001ZZ2Usqihe3aE3m","sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d3ffe8hgDLTRt6IhrOl","messageID":"msg_1db746ace001pt04for4PcP1Yh","type":"tool","id":"call_b17ba83b34f04fbc919b84a9","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"git -c core.fsmonitor=false show 48f03b5013:.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md | sed -n '74,86p'; echo \"---HEAD---\"; sed -n '74,86p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"### Backfill a finished log\n\n`run-command-behaviour.mjs --backfill <run-log> --out <new-log>` adds those three fields to a log written before they existed, and a `--backfill` run without `--out` is a usage error that exits 2. The mode refuses with exit 2 and a JSON body holding its `code`:\n\n- `same_path` when `--out` resolves to the input log, because the backfill writes a new file.\n- `holdout_row` or `unknown_row` when the corpus refuses a row id, because every prompt is resolved before the first line is written and a refused row leaves no output file behind.\n\nA line whose locator names no checkout keeps null offer fields and `offerError` `no_checkout`, and the rest of the log is still written with `offerBackfilled: true`.\n\nA line whose checkout is neither this project root nor an arena holding the `skilled-behaviour-arena` marker also keeps null offer fields, with `offerError` `untrusted_checkout`, because a run log is input and the folder it names may hold any code. Nothing from that folder runs, and the rest of the log is still written.\n\n`--brief-only` keeps every offer field exactly as the input line holds it, present or absent, and recomputes only `briefDelivered`, because a recorded offer belongs to the head the turn saw and replaying it would describe a different head. Brief delivery now comes from the session records of Pi, Devin, DSH and Codex, while OpenCode stays `unknown` because its plugin adds the brief in memory and the store keeps no copy.\n\n---HEAD---\n### Backfill a finished log\n\n`run-command-behaviour.mjs --backfill <run-log> --out <new-log>` adds those four fields to a log written before they existed, and a `--backfill` run without `--out` is a usage error that exits 2. The mode refuses with exit 2 and a JSON body holding its `code`:\n\n- `same_path` when `--out` resolves to the input log, because the backfill writes a new file.\n- `holdout_row` or `unknown_row` when the corpus refuses a row id, because every prompt is resolved before the first line is written and a refused row leaves no output file behind.\n\nA line whose locator names no checkout keeps null offer fields and `offerError` `no_checkout`, and the rest of the log is still written with `offerBackfilled: true`.\n\nA line whose checkout is neither this project root nor an arena holding the `skilled-behaviour-arena` marker also keeps null offer fields, with `offerError` `untrusted_checkout`, because a run log is input and the folder it names may hold any code. Nothing from that folder runs, and the rest of the log is still written.\n\n`--brief-only` keeps every offer field exactly as the input line holds it, present or absent, and recomputes only `briefDelivered`, because a recorded offer belongs to the head the turn saw and replaying it would describe a different head. Brief delivery now comes from the session records of Pi, Devin, DSH and Codex, while OpenCode stays `unknown` because its plugin adds the brief in memory and the store keeps no copy.\n\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"### Backfill a finished log\n\n`run-command-behaviour.mjs --backfill <run-log> --out <new-log>` adds those three fields to a log written before they existed, and a `--backfill` run without `--out` is a usage error that exits 2. The mode refuses with exit 2 and a JSON body holding its `code`:\n\n- `same_path` when `--out` resolves to the input log, because the backfill writes a new file.\n- `holdout_row` or `unknown_row` when the corpus refuses a row id, because every prompt is resolved before the first line is written and a refused row leaves no output file behind.\n\nA line whose locator names no checkout keeps null offer fields and `offerError` `no_checkout`, and the rest of the log is still written with `offerBackfilled: true`.\n\nA line whose checkout is neither this project root nor an arena holding the `skilled-behaviour-arena` marker also keeps null offer fields, with `offerError` `untrusted_checkout`, because a run log is input and the folder it names may hold any code. Nothing from that folder runs, and the rest of the log is still written.\n\n`--brief-only` keeps every offer field exactly as the input line holds it, present or absent, and recomputes only `briefDelivered`, because a recorded offer belongs to the head the turn saw and replaying it would describe a different head. Brief delivery now comes from the session records of Pi, Devin, DSH and Codex, while OpenCode stays `unknown` because its plugin adds the brief in memory and the store keeps no copy.\n\n---HEAD---\n### Backfill a finished log\n\n`run-command-behaviour.mjs --backfill <run-log> --out <new-log>` adds those four fields to a log written before they existed, and a `--backfill` run without `--out` is a usage error that exits 2. The mode refuses with exit 2 and a JSON body holding its `code`:\n\n- `same_path` when `--out` resolves to the input log, because the backfill writes a new file.\n- `holdout_row` or `unknown_row` when the corpus refuses a row id, because every prompt is resolved before the first line is written and a refused row leaves no output file behind.\n\nA line whose locator names no checkout keeps null offer fields and `offerError` `no_checkout`, and the rest of the log is still written with `offerBackfilled: true`.\n\nA line whose checkout is neither this project root nor an arena holding the `skilled-behaviour-arena` marker also keeps null offer fields, with `offerError` `untrusted_checkout`, because a run log is input and the folder it names may hold any code. Nothing from that folder runs, and the rest of the log is still written.\n\n`--brief-only` keeps every offer field exactly as the input line holds it, present or absent, and recomputes only `briefDelivered`, because a recorded offer belongs to the head the turn saw and replaying it would describe a different head. Brief delivery now comes from the session records of Pi, Devin, DSH and Codex, while OpenCode stays `unknown` because its plugin adds the brief in memory and the store keeps no copy.\n\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"git -c core.fsmonitor=false show 48f03b5013:.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md | sed -n '74,86p'; echo \\\"---HEAD---\\\"; sed -n '74,86p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794683226020,"end":1794683227077}}}}
