restates each moved start figure in rows that state the limits | `rescore-delta.txt` of T021 holds 23 start and 11 workflow lines, both `cmp` pairs exit 0, and the `rg` over `../goal.md` prints the new rows | Unmet | - |\n61:| AC-006 | REQ-006 | Given `Is the /doctor:update command safe?` and `the next step is the /speckit:implement command`, When the mention reader reads them, Then the first reads as a question and the second as a request, and the CLI prints no `/doctor:update` row for the first | The rows of T005 failed before and passed after, and the second `rg` of T020 prints nothing | Unmet | - |\n62:| AC-007 | REQ-007 | Given a link inside the Codex store that points at a rollout, When `loadSession` reads it, Then the reader opens the resolved path and never the link, and the reader and history lookup tests pass | The case of T010 failed before and passed after, `RT` and `HT` pass in T018, and `RACE` prints `APPROVED-FILE` in T020 | Unmet | - |\n63:| AC-008 | REQ-008 | Given heredocs whose end words are `END-SCRIPT` and `END.JS`, When `workflowPath` reads them, Then each returns `none` | The rows of T008 failed before and passed after, and every `heredoc` line of `SHELLP` in T020 ends in `improvised` | Unmet | - |\n64:| AC-009 | REQ-009 | Given a made-up capture that publishes three holdout ids, When `publishedHoldoutIds` reads it, Then it returns the three ids, and the guard reads both the committed baseline and the live capture | The case of T011 failed before and passed after, and the slice test passes in T018 | Unmet | - |\n65:| AC-010 | REQ-010 | Given the five documents, When each is searched for its new sentence, Then each names the behaviour the code has | The `rg` checks of T012 to T017 | Unmet | - |\n66:| AC-011 | REQ-011 | Given the fix commit, When the confirming round runs and every P0 and P1 is adjudicated, Then each lineage ends at or below 0.10 with 0 adjudicated P1, or the last round closes with a written judgment, and `../review/review-report.md` holds counts from pass-four lineages only | `review-rounds.txt` and the goal log row of T025, and the report checks of T026 | Unmet | - |\n67:| AC-012 | REQ-012 | Given the phase diff, When added comment lines are searched for a spec path or an id and the row files, the baseline, `AGENTS.md` and the package files are checked, Then nothing is found and nothing outside `FILES` changed | The checks of T022 | Unmet | - |\n91:<!-- FILL: Write Yes or No and one sentence. Name a criterion by its id only when it blocks closure. Never write a count of criteria or an id range, because every added row makes it wrong. GOOD: No. AC-002 is unmet. WEAK: All eight criteria AC-001 to AC-008 are met. -->\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"Acceptance\\\\|AC-\\\\|CHK-FIX\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/acceptance-criteria.md | head -50\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794683240653,"end":1794683241411}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794683241418,"sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d3ffe8hgDLTRt6IhrOl","part":{"partID":"prt_1db74fd22001dGHhIWL5e7e2Vk","sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d3ffe8hgDLTRt6IhrOl","messageID":"msg_1db74d1a9001Lw5aNnJWgr777U","type":"tool","id":"call_2d2013696fea4016bcde5853","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"pair\\|shared owned\\|unscoredOnly\\|stored run line\\|offeredAs\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md | head -40","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"52:- Two run-log writers that keep `offeredAs`.\n64:A reader who writes `do not run /create:agent or /create:readme` still gets `/create:readme (start)` on the top row, and a reader who asks `Is the /doctor:update command safe?` gets `/doctor:update (ask)`. Phase 026 would also measure on harness faults: neither run-log writer keeps `offeredAs`, so a command shown on the partner side of an ambiguous head counts as offered, and a run that reads a command document through the shell and then writes reads as not started, which hides 12 starts in the stored arms and would hide them again in 864 new sessions.\n106:parseOffer {\"offeredCommand\":\"/create:manual-testing-playbook\",\"offeredPolicy\":\"start\",\"offeredAs\":\"partner\"}\n107:backfill true keys [\"runtime\",\"rowId\",\"arm\",\"exit\",\"locator\",\"offeredCommand\",\"offeredPolicy\",\"offerError\",\"briefDelivered\",\"offerBackfilled\"] NO offeredAs\n204:| iter1-P1-offeredas-not-persisted | `backfillRunLog` (`RAD/command-offer.mjs:490-497`) and `runTurn` (`RAD/run-command-behaviour.mjs:1183-1187`) copy the offer's command and policy and drop `offeredAs` | Fix (T006, T007). Stored lines get no backfill, because the head a stored run saw cannot be replayed from today's code |\n214:| iter3-P2-pair-doc-shared-rows, iter4-P2-paired-arm-key-collision, iter4-P2-unscored-only-dead-field | The pair block, the arm name `paired` and `unscoredOnly` live in code phase 026 rewrites | Deferred to phase 026 T030, T053 and T052 (P046) |\n229:- Keep `offeredAs` on every run line both writers write. The runner gains one exported helper, `offerLineFields`, because `runTurn` is not exported and a dry run is refused on a dirty tree, so no test could reach the line otherwise.\n235:- A backfill of `offeredAs` onto stored run lines - a replay today prints today's head, not the one the run saw.\n238:- The pair README sentence, the reserved arm name `paired` and the dead `unscoredOnly` count - phase 026 rewrites the same functions (P046).\n250:| `RAD/command-offer.mjs` | Modify | `backfillRunLog` writes `offeredAs` |\n259:| `RAD/README.md` | Modify | `offeredAs` in both field lists, the start rule and the heredoc end word |\n280:| REQ-002 | A backfilled line and a live run line carry `offeredAs` as `head`, `partner` or `null`, as the replayed offer gives it. |\n293:| REQ-010 | The routing-accuracy README lists `offeredAs` in both field lists and states the shell-read start rule and the heredoc end word, the advisor README names `parent-named only`, `advisor-recommend.md` states that the head keeps its command, `command-meaning-matching.md` reads 28 cases and the agents-md presentation names the by-hand fix for a malformed A11 row. |\n308:- **SC-002**: `node $PRB/offeredas-backfill.mjs <temp folder>` prints `HAS offeredAs`, where it printed `NO offeredAs`.\n347:- **NFR-R01**: A run line written before this phase still scores as before, because a line with no `offeredAs` keeps its offer count.\n355:- Empty input: a replay that fails writes `offeredAs: null` beside its null command, and a shell event with no command text adds no start.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"52:- Two run-log writers that keep `offeredAs`.\n64:A reader who writes `do not run /create:agent or /create:readme` still gets `/create:readme (start)` on the top row, and a reader who asks `Is the /doctor:update command safe?` gets `/doctor:update (ask)`. Phase 026 would also measure on harness faults: neither run-log writer keeps `offeredAs`, so a command shown on the partner side of an ambiguous head counts as offered, and a run that reads a command document through the shell and then writes reads as not started, which hides 12 starts in the stored arms and would hide them again in 864 new sessions.\n106:parseOffer {\"offeredCommand\":\"/create:manual-testing-playbook\",\"offeredPolicy\":\"start\",\"offeredAs\":\"partner\"}\n107:backfill true keys [\"runtime\",\"rowId\",\"arm\",\"exit\",\"locator\",\"offeredCommand\",\"offeredPolicy\",\"offerError\",\"briefDelivered\",\"offerBackfilled\"] NO offeredAs\n204:| iter1-P1-offeredas-not-persisted | `backfillRunLog` (`RAD/command-offer.mjs:490-497`) and `runTurn` (`RAD/run-command-behaviour.mjs:1183-1187`) copy the offer's command and policy and drop `offeredAs` | Fix (T006, T007). Stored lines get no backfill, because the head a stored run saw cannot be replayed from today's code |\n214:| iter3-P2-pair-doc-shared-rows, iter4-P2-paired-arm-key-collision, iter4-P2-unscored-only-dead-field | The pair block, the arm name `paired` and `unscoredOnly` live in code phase 026 rewrites | Deferred to phase 026 T030, T053 and T052 (P046) |\n229:- Keep `offeredAs` on every run line both writers write. The runner gains one exported helper, `offerLineFields`, because `runTurn` is not exported and a dry run is refused on a dirty tree, so no test could reach the line otherwise.\n235:- A backfill of `offeredAs` onto stored run lines - a replay today prints today's head, not the one the run saw.\n238:- The pair README sentence, the reserved arm name `paired` and the dead `unscoredOnly` count - phase 026 rewrites the same functions (P046).\n250:| `RAD/command-offer.mjs` | Modify | `backfillRunLog` writes `offeredAs` |\n259:| `RAD/README.md` | Modify | `offeredAs` in both field lists, the start rule and the heredoc end word |\n280:| REQ-002 | A backfilled line and a live run line carry `offeredAs` as `head`, `partner` or `null`, as the replayed offer gives it. |\n293:| REQ-010 | The routing-accuracy README lists `offeredAs` in both field lists and states the shell-read start rule and the heredoc end word, the advisor README names `parent-named only`, `advisor-recommend.md` states that the head keeps its command, `command-meaning-matching.md` reads 28 cases and the agents-md presentation names the by-hand fix for a malformed A11 row. |\n308:- **SC-002**: `node $PRB/offeredas-backfill.mjs <temp folder>` prints `HAS offeredAs`, where it printed `NO offeredAs`.\n347:- **NFR-R01**: A run line written before this phase still scores as before, because a line with no `offeredAs` keeps its offer count.\n355:- Empty input: a replay that fails writes `offeredAs: null` beside its null command, and a shell event with no command text adds no start.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"pair\\\\|shared owned\\\\|unscoredOnly\\\\|stored run line\\\\|offeredAs\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md | head -40\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794683239714,"end":1794683241418}}}}
