{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794683272052,"sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d3ffe8hgDLTRt6IhrOl","part":{"partID":"prt_1db7578ed001iI9IK0rkMWWZpf","sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d3ffe8hgDLTRt6IhrOl","messageID":"msg_1db750868001T1nBXA02U1dvo6","type":"tool","id":"call_d6094169e1984073b292b79f","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"offerError\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md | head -10","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"72:The offer is a replay of the Claude prompt hook after the turn instead of a copy of the live session head. The head is the only text that names both the command and the policy, and not every runtime keeps it, so `replayOffer` runs the checkout's own hook and records what that checkout would have offered at the time of the run. A replay that finds no hook, a failing hook or a head without an offer writes null fields plus an `offerError` of `hook_missing`, `hook_failed` or `no_head`, so one bad line never aborts a run.\n81:A line whose locator names no checkout keeps null offer fields and `offerError` `no_checkout`, and the rest of the log is still written with `offerBackfilled: true`.\n83:A line whose checkout is neither this project root nor an arena holding the `skilled-behaviour-arena` marker also keeps null offer fields, with `offerError` `untrusted_checkout`, because a run log is input and the folder it names may hold any code. Nothing from that folder runs, and the rest of the log is still written.\n188:The output log holds the same lines plus `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs`, `offerError`, `briefDelivered` and `offerBackfilled`. Exit 2 means the output was refused, and the printed JSON names why: `same_path`, `holdout_row`, `unknown_row` or a missing `--out`.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"72:The offer is a replay of the Claude prompt hook after the turn instead of a copy of the live session head. The head is the only text that names both the command and the policy, and not every runtime keeps it, so `replayOffer` runs the checkout's own hook and records what that checkout would have offered at the time of the run. A replay that finds no hook, a failing hook or a head without an offer writes null fields plus an `offerError` of `hook_missing`, `hook_failed` or `no_head`, so one bad line never aborts a run.\n81:A line whose locator names no checkout keeps null offer fields and `offerError` `no_checkout`, and the rest of the log is still written with `offerBackfilled: true`.\n83:A line whose checkout is neither this project root nor an arena holding the `skilled-behaviour-arena` marker also keeps null offer fields, with `offerError` `untrusted_checkout`, because a run log is input and the folder it names may hold any code. Nothing from that folder runs, and the rest of the log is still written.\n188:The output log holds the same lines plus `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs`, `offerError`, `briefDelivered` and `offerBackfilled`. Exit 2 means the output was refused, and the printed JSON names why: `same_path`, `holdout_row`, `unknown_row` or a missing `--out`.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"offerError\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md | head -10\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794683271405,"end":1794683272052}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794683272075,"sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d3ffe8hgDLTRt6IhrOl","part":{"partID":"prt_1db7574da0015UW9Mvdd3vBV88","sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d3ffe8hgDLTRt6IhrOl","messageID":"msg_1db750868001T1nBXA02U1dvo6","type":"tool","id":"call_2a38eed504e6467c809c3fc7","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"offerError\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs; echo \"---48f---\"; git -c core.fsmonitor=false show 48f03b5013:.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs | sed -n '1188,1210p'","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"---48f---\n  // honestly report as left as found.\n  const restore = options.dryRun ? null : restoreTurn({ cwd: REPO_ROOT, before: before.status });\n  const restored = options.dryRun ? changed.length === 0 : restore.restored;\n  // The head the reader saw is the only place the offer was named, and not every\n  // runtime keeps it, so the offer is replayed after the turn. A dry run still\n  // replays it, which lets an operator read the offer without paying for a model\n  // call, while the brief stays `unknown` because no session exists to read.\n  const offer = replayOffer({ checkoutDir: PROJECT_DIR, prompt: job.prompt, sessionId });\n  // Pi, Devin and DSH keep the brief in their session store rather than in the\n  // turn records, so the delivery check needs the reader that opens that store.\n  const delivered = options.dryRun\n    ? 'unknown'\n    : await briefDelivered({ runtime: job.runtimeName, locator, loadSession: loadSharedSession });\n  appendRunLine(options.out, {\n    ...line,\n    ...offerLineFields(offer),\n    briefDelivered: delivered,\n    restored,\n    ...(restore !== null && restore.leftoverPaths.length > 0\n      ? { leftoverPaths: restore.leftoverPaths }\n      : {}),\n  });\n\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"---48f---\n  // honestly report as left as found.\n  const restore = options.dryRun ? null : restoreTurn({ cwd: REPO_ROOT, before: before.status });\n  const restored = options.dryRun ? changed.length === 0 : restore.restored;\n  // The head the reader saw is the only place the offer was named, and not every\n  // runtime keeps it, so the offer is replayed after the turn. A dry run still\n  // replays it, which lets an operator read the offer without paying for a model\n  // call, while the brief stays `unknown` because no session exists to read.\n  const offer = replayOffer({ checkoutDir: PROJECT_DIR, prompt: job.prompt, sessionId });\n  // Pi, Devin and DSH keep the brief in their session store rather than in the\n  // turn records, so the delivery check needs the reader that opens that store.\n  const delivered = options.dryRun\n    ? 'unknown'\n    : await briefDelivered({ runtime: job.runtimeName, locator, loadSession: loadSharedSession });\n  appendRunLine(options.out, {\n    ...line,\n    ...offerLineFields(offer),\n    briefDelivered: delivered,\n    restored,\n    ...(restore !== null && restore.leftoverPaths.length > 0\n      ? { leftoverPaths: restore.leftoverPaths }\n      : {}),\n  });\n\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"offerError\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs; echo \\\"---48f---\\\"; git -c core.fsmonitor=false show 48f03b5013:.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs | sed -n '1188,1210p'\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794683270362,"end":1794683272075}}}}
