{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794683566404,"sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d3ffe8hgDLTRt6IhrOl","part":{"partID":"prt_1db79af7d00162gA2xRimvJW7R","sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d3ffe8hgDLTRt6IhrOl","messageID":"msg_1db798a3c001lSDJrhSIhO2d1w","type":"tool","id":"call_8c0c727a3c6d4880a5d53a35","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"---\ntitle: Deep Review Strategy - accuracy-runner-close-4c lineage\ndescription: Runtime strategy tracking the closing review of pass-four fixes in the accuracy-runner area of command surfacing.\nversion: 1.11.14.0\n---\n\n# Deep Review Strategy - accuracy-runner-close-4c lineage\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nPersistent brain for this fan-out lineage. It records which dimensions remain, what was found\n(P0/P1/P2), which review approaches worked or failed, and where to focus next. Read at every\niteration before any review action.\n\n### Ownership\n\nMachine-managed metrics and coverage blocks are wrapped in explicit ownership anchors. Human\ncommentary and operator overrides live outside those anchors.\n\n---\n\n## 2. TOPIC\n\nClosing round of review pass four of `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`\nin the `accuracy-runner` area. The changed accuracy-runner path in `review/review-scope-4c.txt`\nis the routing-accuracy `README.md`; the brief's checks also name the run-log writers, the\ntranscript scorer, the Codex reader and the holdout guard as verification surfaces. The change\nrange is `48f03b5013..868b185e76`.\n\nThe operator focus is the closing brief: read `review-brief-4c.txt` first; confirm that a refusal\nover an or-list, with or without the article and the word command, and a question over an or-list\ncarry no command while a request over a list keeps its command; that both run-log writers keep\n`offeredAs`; that a shell read of a command document counts as a start while a search, an in-place\n`sed`, a redirect and a heredoc line do not; that a heredoc end word with a hyphen or a dot closes\ncorrectly; that the Codex reader opens the resolved file; that the holdout guard reads the live\ncapture; and that docs agree with code. Holdout prompt text is never read or printed.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n- [ ] correctness\n- [ ] security\n- [ ] traceability\n- [ ] maintainability\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- The mention reader in `lib/command-attach.ts`, the scorer fusion, the recommend handler and the\n  feature docs belong to the `scorer-attach-close-4c` lineage. This lineage reads them only as\n  context evidence and raises no finding against them.\n- The deferred pair-doc sentence, the reserved `paired` arm name and the `unscoredOnly` field are\n  phase 026 work per `027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md`; they are not re-reported here.\n- Holdout prompt text is never read or printed. Corpus work is limited to counts and\n  `jq 'del(.prompt)'` rows.\n- No code changes: review is observation-only.\n- No runtime command, build, test run or generator is executed; every claim is grounded in a\n  direct file read of the fixed tree.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Convergence: `newFindingsRatio` at or below the 0.10 threshold with no active P0.\n- Cap: `maxIterations` 2.\n- Stuck: two consecutive iterations with no new evidence (stuckThreshold 2).\n- Any active P0 blocks PASS regardless of convergence.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n[None yet -- populated as iterations complete dimension reviews]\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n## 7. RUNNING FINDINGS\n- P0 (Blockers): 0\n- P1 (Required): 0\n- P2 (Suggestions): 0\n- Resolved: 0\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n\n---\n\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n[Populated when a review approach has been tried from multiple angles without yielding new findings]\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n\n---\n\n## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Swept: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n\n## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n\n- [Populated when an iteration rules a direction out, with its evidence]\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 12. NEXT FOCUS\n- Dimension: correctness and security - Focus area: the five behaviour checks the brief names: both run-log writers keep `offeredAs`, a shell read counts as a start while a search, an in-place `sed`, a redirect and a heredoc line do not, a heredoc end word with a hyphen or a dot closes, the Codex reader opens the resolved file, and the holdout guard reads the live capture - Reason: the first pass verifies the fixed code before the docs pass interprets it - Rotation status: correctness and security start now; traceability and maintainability follow - Required evidence: direct reads of the writers, `readDocument`, `HEREDOC_BODY`, `loadCodexSession` and `publishedHoldoutIds`, plus the README lines that describe them - Blocked/productive carry-forward: none - Recovery note: none\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n\n---\n\n## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\n\n- Target pointers: the accuracy-runner `README.md` line in `review/review-scope-4c.txt`; the\n  verification surfaces named by the brief (`command-offer.mjs`, `run-command-behaviour.mjs`,\n  `score-command-transcripts.mjs`, `codex.mjs`, `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts`); the 4c fix\n  commit `868b185e76`; the verify report `review/verify-4/report.md`; the 4b adjudication\n  `027-review-pass-four-remediation/scratch/review-rounds.txt`.\n- Behavior claims: `offeredAs` travels through both run-log writers; a shell read of a command\n  document starts it while a search, an in-place `sed`, a redirect and a heredoc line do not; an\n  end word with a hyphen or a dot closes a heredoc; the Codex reader opens the containment-resolved\n  path; the holdout guard checks the live capture; a refusal or question over an or-list carries\n  no command while a request keeps it.\n- Reuse and conventions: the reviewer containment pattern already used by `claude.mjs`; the\n  `P0/P1/P2` scale; the delta plus iteration narrative pair; the append gateway as sole state-log\n  writer; the reducer-owned registry and dashboard.\n- Review risks and gaps: no live per-runtime session was captured in this lineage, so runtime\n  behaviour is read from code, tests and the 027 evidence. The mention reader is the sibling\n  lineage's surface. The holdout corpus is not opened.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-reference-status -->\n## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n|----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n| `spec_code` | core | pending | - | Phase 027 T006-T013 and T030 are the code and doc claims under check. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | - | `CHK-040` and the 027 acceptance rows name the offeredAs and doc claims. |\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pending | - | No agent definition changed in this area. |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pending | - | The Codex reader is the one runtime-specific surface in scope. |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | - | No feature-catalog page describes the changed accuracy-runner lines. |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | pending | - | No playbook surface changed. |\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-reference-status -->\n\n---\n\n## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\n\n| File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\n|------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md` | pending | - | 0 | pending |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs` | pending | - | 0 | pending |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs` | pending | - | 0 | pending |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs` | pending | - | 0 | pending |\n| `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/codex.mjs` | pending | - | 0 | pending |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` | pending | - | 0 | pending |\n\n---\n\n## 16. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\n\n- Max iterations: 2\n- Convergence threshold: 0.10\n- Rolling STOP threshold: 0.08\n- No-progress threshold: 0.05\n- Coverage stabilization passes required: 1\n- Session lineage: sessionId=fanout-accuracy-runner-close-4c-1794682797954-pcdanq,\n  parentSessionId=null, generation=1, lineageMode=new\n- Findings registry: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`\n- Release-readiness states: in-progress | converged | release-blocking\n- Per-iteration budget: 12 tool calls, 10 minutes\n- Severity threshold: P2\n- Review target type: spec-folder\n- Cross-reference checks: core=[spec_code, checklist_evidence],\n  overlay=[skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_capability]\n- Started: 2026-11-14T19:11:54Z\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-close-4c/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-close-4c/deep-review-strategy.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-close-4c/deep-review-strategy.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"---\\ntitle: Deep Review Strategy - accuracy-runner-close-4c lineage\\ndescription: Runtime strategy tracking the closing review of pass-four fixes in the accuracy-runner area of command surfacing.\\nversion: 1.11.14.0\\n---\\n\\n# Deep Review Strategy - accuracy-runner-close-4c lineage\\n\\n## 1. OVERVIEW\\n\\n### Purpose\\n\\nPersistent brain for this fan-out lineage. It records which dimensions remain, what was found\\n(P0/P1/P2), which review approaches worked or failed, and where to focus next. Read at every\\niteration before any review action.\\n\\n### Ownership\\n\\nMachine-managed metrics and coverage blocks are wrapped in explicit ownership anchors. Human\\ncommentary and operator overrides live outside those anchors.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. TOPIC\\n\\nClosing round of review pass four of `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`\\nin the `accuracy-runner` area. The changed accuracy-runner path in `review/review-scope-4c.txt`\\nis the routing-accuracy `README.md`; the brief's checks also name the run-log writers, the\\ntranscript scorer, the Codex reader and the holdout guard as verification surfaces. The change\\nrange is `48f03b5013..868b185e76`.\\n\\nThe operator focus is the closing brief: read `review-brief-4c.txt` first; confirm that a refusal\\nover an or-list, with or without the article and the word command, and a question over an or-list\\ncarry no command while a request over a list keeps its command; that both run-log writers keep\\n`offeredAs`; that a shell read of a command document counts as a start while a search, an in-place\\n`sed`, a redirect and a heredoc line do not; that a heredoc end word with a hyphen or a dot closes\\ncorrectly; that the Codex reader opens the resolved file; that the holdout guard reads the live\\ncapture; and that docs agree with code. Holdout prompt text is never read or printed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\\n- [ ] correctness\\n- [ ] security\\n- [ ] traceability\\n- [ ] maintainability\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. NON-GOALS\\n\\n- The mention reader in `lib/command-attach.ts`, the scorer fusion, the recommend handler and the\\n  feature docs belong to the `scorer-attach-close-4c` lineage. This lineage reads them only as\\n  context evidence and raises no finding against them.\\n- The deferred pair-doc sentence, the reserved `paired` arm name and the `unscoredOnly` field are\\n  phase 026 work per `027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md`; they are not re-reported here.\\n- Holdout prompt text is never read or printed. Corpus work is limited to counts and\\n  `jq 'del(.prompt)'` rows.\\n- No code changes: review is observation-only.\\n- No runtime command, build, test run or generator is executed; every claim is grounded in a\\n  direct file read of the fixed tree.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\\n\\n- Convergence: `newFindingsRatio` at or below the 0.10 threshold with no active P0.\\n- Cap: `maxIterations` 2.\\n- Stuck: two consecutive iterations with no new evidence (stuckThreshold 2).\\n- Any active P0 blocks PASS regardless of convergence.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\\n## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\\n[None yet -- populated as iterations complete dimension reviews]\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\\n## 7. RUNNING FINDINGS\\n- P0 (Blockers): 0\\n- P1 (Required): 0\\n- P2 (Suggestions): 0\\n- Resolved: 0\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n- [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\\n[Populated when a review approach has been tried from multiple angles without yielding new findings]\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\\n- Completed pivots: 0\\n- Failed pivots: 0\\n- Audited overrides: 0\\n- Swept: none yet\\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\\n\\n## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\\n\\n- [Populated when an iteration rules a direction out, with its evidence]\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n## 12. NEXT FOCUS\\n- Dimension: correctness and security - Focus area: the five behaviour checks the brief names: both run-log writers keep `offeredAs`, a shell read counts as a start while a search, an in-place `sed`, a redirect and a heredoc line do not, a heredoc end word with a hyphen or a dot closes, the Codex reader opens the resolved file, and the holdout guard reads the live capture - Reason: the first pass verifies the fixed code before the docs pass interprets it - Rotation status: correctness and security start now; traceability and maintainability follow - Required evidence: direct reads of the writers, `readDocument`, `HEREDOC_BODY`, `loadCodexSession` and `publishedHoldoutIds`, plus the README lines that describe them - Blocked/productive carry-forward: none - Recovery note: none\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\\n\\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\\n\\n- Target pointers: the accuracy-runner `README.md` line in `review/review-scope-4c.txt`; the\\n  verification surfaces named by the brief (`command-offer.mjs`, `run-command-behaviour.mjs`,\\n  `score-command-transcripts.mjs`, `codex.mjs`, `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts`); the 4c fix\\n  commit `868b185e76`; the verify report `review/verify-4/report.md`; the 4b adjudication\\n  `027-review-pass-four-remediation/scratch/review-rounds.txt`.\\n- Behavior claims: `offeredAs` travels through both run-log writers; a shell read of a command\\n  document starts it while a search, an in-place `sed`, a redirect and a heredoc line do not; an\\n  end word with a hyphen or a dot closes a heredoc; the Codex reader opens the containment-resolved\\n  path; the holdout guard checks the live capture; a refusal or question over an or-list carries\\n  no command while a request keeps it.\\n- Reuse and conventions: the reviewer containment pattern already used by `claude.mjs`; the\\n  `P0/P1/P2` scale; the delta plus iteration narrative pair; the append gateway as sole state-log\\n  writer; the reducer-owned registry and dashboard.\\n- Review risks and gaps: no live per-runtime session was captured in this lineage, so runtime\\n  behaviour is read from code, tests and the 027 evidence. The mention reader is the sibling\\n  lineage's surface. The holdout corpus is not opened.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-reference-status -->\\n## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\\n|----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\\n| `spec_code` | core | pending | - | Phase 027 T006-T013 and T030 are the code and doc claims under check. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | - | `CHK-040` and the 027 acceptance rows name the offeredAs and doc claims. |\\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pending | - | No agent definition changed in this area. |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pending | - | The Codex reader is the one runtime-specific surface in scope. |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | - | No feature-catalog page describes the changed accuracy-runner lines. |\\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | pending | - | No playbook surface changed. |\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-reference-status -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\\n\\n| File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\\n|------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md` | pending | - | 0 | pending |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs` | pending | - | 0 | pending |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs` | pending | - | 0 | pending |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs` | pending | - | 0 | pending |\\n| `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/codex.mjs` | pending | - | 0 | pending |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` | pending | - | 0 | pending |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 16. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\\n\\n- Max iterations: 2\\n- Convergence threshold: 0.10\\n- Rolling STOP threshold: 0.08\\n- No-progress threshold: 0.05\\n- Coverage stabilization passes required: 1\\n- Session lineage: sessionId=fanout-accuracy-runner-close-4c-1794682797954-pcdanq,\\n  parentSessionId=null, generation=1, lineageMode=new\\n- Findings registry: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`\\n- Release-readiness states: in-progress | converged | release-blocking\\n- Per-iteration budget: 12 tool calls, 10 minutes\\n- Severity threshold: P2\\n- Review target type: spec-folder\\n- Cross-reference checks: core=[spec_code, checklist_evidence],\\n  overlay=[skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_capability]\\n- Started: 2026-11-14T19:11:54Z\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-close-4c/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794683547517,"end":1794683566404}}}}
