{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794683641498,"sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d3ffe8hgDLTRt6IhrOl","part":{"partID":"prt_1db7b1d190016rH55xheexuvEK","sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d3ffe8hgDLTRt6IhrOl","messageID":"msg_1db7a86e5001F0JckR3wrJHiKD","type":"tool","id":"call_0ad1bf4bb2824e4aa435ca1e","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-4b/iterations/iteration-003.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-4b/iterations/iteration-003.md, lines 1-140\n1: # Review Iteration 3\n2: \n3: - Mode: review\n4: - Lineage: `accuracy-runner-confirm-4b`\n5: - Run: `fanout-accuracy-runner-confirm-4b-1794680176420-xvj4ed`\n6: - Iteration: 3 of 3\n7: - Dimension: RECOVERY (least-covered traceability and maintainability)\n8: - Budget profile: adjudicate (8-10 read actions)\n9: - Sources read: `review-brief-4b.txt`, `steer.md` (absent), `review/verify-4/report.md`, phase 027 `tasks.md`, the iteration-2 narrative\n10: \n11: ## Dispatcher\n12: \n13: `/deep:review` fan-out lineage `accuracy-runner-confirm-4b`. The recovery pass changes\n14: granularity from code to line-level doc claims. It checks the two shared docs this area changed\n15: (`routing-accuracy/README.md` and `doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt`) against the code and the\n16: task rows that claim them.\n17: \n18: ## Files Reviewed\n19: \n20: - `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:63-80,120-126,183-188`\n21: - `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt:255-272`\n22: - `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:1170-1209`\n23: - `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:84-110,218-244`\n24: \n25: Context reads: `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:757-808` and\n26: `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:373-410,782-803` for the A11 claim;\n27: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:488-501`\n28: for the backfill field set.\n29: \n30: ## Findings - New\n31: \n32: ### P0 Findings\n33: \n34: None.\n35: \n36: ### P1 Findings\n37: \n38: None.\n39: \n40: ### P2 Findings\n41: \n42: 1. **The README still says the backfill adds three fields and lists three in the runner row** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:76` -- The backfill now writes `offeredAs` as a fourth attribution field (`command-offer.mjs:496`, `run-command-behaviour.mjs:824`), and the output sentence at `:188` names it, but the paragraph at `:76` still says \"adds those three fields\" and the `run-command-behaviour.mjs` row at `:125` still says `--backfill` rewrites with `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy` and `briefDelivered`. A reader following the section learns a three-field contract that the code no longer has. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:76]\n43:    Finding class: doc_code_drift\n44:    Scope proof: the README is in the declared accuracy-runner scope; the two code lines are the changed writers, and phase 027 T012 claims the README field lists.\n45:    Affected surface hints: README backfill section, runner table row, the `offeredAs` attribution contract.\n46:    Case: run `node .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs --backfill in.jsonl --out out.jsonl`; every output line carries `offeredAs` (pinned by `command-offer.vitest.ts:385-388`), while `README.md:76` says three fields and `:125` names only three.\n47: \n48: 2. **The README says every run line carries four attribution fields, but a head-moved line carries none** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:65` -- `runTurn` appends the head-moved line before the offer replay at `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1180-1184`, so that line has no `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs` or `briefDelivered`. The blanket sentence is false for the exit-3 path the README itself documents. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:65]\n49:    Finding class: doc_code_drift\n50:    Scope proof: the README and `run-command-behaviour.mjs` are both in the declared scope; the early append is the same writer's own branch.\n51:    Affected surface hints: head-moved run line, exit 3, attribution contract, scorer's `offerFieldAbsent`.\n52:    Case: a turn that commits or stashes during the run sets `headMoved`; `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1183` appends `{ ...line, restored: false, headMoved: true }` and returns exit 3. The written JSON has none of the four fields, while `README.md:65` says each appended line carries them. A scorer reading that line sees `offerFieldAbsent` even though the run line is valid.\n53: \n54: The A11 malformed-router row added at\n55: `doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt:268` agrees with the code: the doctor check reports\n56: `malformed <kind> row at line N: C cells where the header has H`\n57: (`agents-md-check.cjs:776-778`), and the embed only splices missing rows into the table\n58: (`agents-md-embed.cjs:373-410`), so the advice to fix the row by hand matches what embed will\n59: and will not do. No finding.\n60: \n61: ## Traceability Checks\n62: \n63: - `spec_code` -- partial. Phase 027 T006, T007, T010, T012, T013 and T017 are marked `[x]` with\n64:   evidence, and the code matches T006/T007/T010. T012's \"both field lists\" is narrower than the\n65:   README's actual field lists: the backfill paragraph and the runner table row still say three\n66:   fields.\n67: - `checklist_evidence` -- partial. `CHK-040` (tasks.md:244) asks `RA` to name `offeredAs` in both\n68:   field lists; the two lists T012 edited are correct, but the backfill lists are the remaining\n69:   drift. `CHK-FIX-003` and `CHK-FIX-004` remain open with the phase.\n70: - `feature_catalog_code` -- notApplicable. No feature-catalog page describes the two changed\n71:   writers; the routing-accuracy README is the shared doc.\n72: - `agent_cross_runtime` -- notApplicable. No runtime branch in the changed docs or writers.\n73: - `skill_agent` -- notApplicable. No agent definition changed.\n74: - `playbook_capability` -- notApplicable. No playbook surface changed.\n75: \n76: ## Integration Evidence\n77: \n78: - The routing-accuracy README is the only shared doc that describes `command-offer.mjs` and\n79:   `run-command-behaviour.mjs`; phase 027 T012 and T013 edit it as the doc of record.\n80: - The doctor presentation asset is the `/doctor:agents-md` troubleshooting text. Its new row\n81:   points at the same two scripts the doctor check and embed run:\n82:   `agents-md-check.cjs:757-808` and `agents-md-embed.cjs:782-803`.\n83: - The head-moved branch is the same `runTurn` function that now spreads `offerLineFields`; the\n84:   early return at `:1180-1184` is the one path that never reaches the offer replay.\n85: \n86: ## Edge Cases\n87: \n88: - A malformed shipped router row makes the checker report it as malformed and as missing. The\n89:   embed then adds a second, well-formed copy of that shipped row, and the malformed row stays.\n90:   The added A11 advice does not warn about the duplicate; the row still says embed never rewrites\n91:   a row, which is true, and the operator is told to fix the row by hand. Recorded as an operator\n92:   note, not a finding, because the added text does not claim the duplicate cannot happen.\n93: - The backfill's `--brief-only` path leaves a legacy line without `offeredAs`, which the README's\n94:   `--brief-only` paragraph already covers. The stale \"three fields\" paragraph is about the\n95:   default path, so the two statements do not conflict.\n96: - A head-moved line is written before `restoreTurn`, so `leftoverPaths` is absent too. The\n97:   README's head-moved paragraph names only `restored` and the changed paths; this is consistent\n98:   with the line and part of the same all-or-nothing early return.\n99: \n100: ## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n101: \n102: - The A11 malformed-row guidance matches the checker's message and the embed's insert-only\n103:   behavior.\n104: - The top attribution list (`README.md:65-70`) now names four fields, including `offeredAs`.\n105: - The output sentence (`README.md:188`) names `offeredAs` alongside the other backfill fields.\n106: - Phase 027 task rows T006, T007, T010, T012, T013 and T017 are marked `[x]` with evidence that\n107:   matches the changed lines this lineage read.\n108: \n109: ## Ruled Out\n110: \n111: - **The A11 row contradicts the doctor check.** Ruled out: the checker's malformed message names\n112:   the cell count and the header width, and the embed only adds missing rows.\n113: - **The top attribution list still says three fields.** Ruled out: `README.md:65` says four and\n114:   the item at `:69` defines `offeredAs`.\n115: - **The output-log sentence still omits `offeredAs`.** Ruled out: `README.md:188` lists it.\n116: - **The backfill paragraph's \"three fields\" is correct for `--brief-only`.** Ruled out: the\n117:   paragraph introduces the default backfill, and the separate `--brief-only` paragraph is the\n118:   one that describes copying offer fields untouched.\n119: \n120: ## Next Focus\n121: \n122: - Dimension: none remaining within the cap; synthesis\n123: - Focus area: compile the lineage report from the registry, the three deltas and the\n124:   documentation findings.\n125: - Reason: three iterations are complete, two clean code dimensions and two P2 doc drifts; the\n126:   cap is reached without a legal convergence stop.\n127: - Rotation status: correctness and security complete; traceability and maintainability covered by\n128:   the recovery pass (partial, because the packet's checklist is still open).\n129: - Required evidence: the registry's active counts, the three iteration final lines and the\n130:   synthesis report.\n131: - Blocked/productive carry-forward: no blocked approach.\n132: - Recovery note: the recovery pass changed granularity to line-level doc claims and produced the\n133:   two findings.\n134: \n135: ## Verdict\n136: \n137: No active P0 or P1 finding. Two P2 documentation drifts remain active; the verdict is PASS with\n138: advisories.\n139: \n140: Review verdict: PASS","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-4b/iterations/iteration-003.md, lines 1-140\n1: # Review Iteration 3\n2: \n3: - Mode: review\n4: - Lineage: `accuracy-runner-confirm-4b`\n5: - Run: `fanout-accuracy-runner-confirm-4b-1794680176420-xvj4ed`\n6: - Iteration: 3 of 3\n7: - Dimension: RECOVERY (least-covered traceability and maintainability)\n8: - Budget profile: adjudicate (8-10 read actions)\n9: - Sources read: `review-brief-4b.txt`, `steer.md` (absent), `review/verify-4/report.md`, phase 027 `tasks.md`, the iteration-2 narrative\n10: \n11: ## Dispatcher\n12: \n13: `/deep:review` fan-out lineage `accuracy-runner-confirm-4b`. The recovery pass changes\n14: granularity from code to line-level doc claims. It checks the two shared docs this area changed\n15: (`routing-accuracy/README.md` and `doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt`) against the code and the\n16: task rows that claim them.\n17: \n18: ## Files Reviewed\n19: \n20: - `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:63-80,120-126,183-188`\n21: - `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt:255-272`\n22: - `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:1170-1209`\n23: - `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:84-110,218-244`\n24: \n25: Context reads: `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:757-808` and\n26: `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:373-410,782-803` for the A11 claim;\n27: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:488-501`\n28: for the backfill field set.\n29: \n30: ## Findings - New\n31: \n32: ### P0 Findings\n33: \n34: None.\n35: \n36: ### P1 Findings\n37: \n38: None.\n39: \n40: ### P2 Findings\n41: \n42: 1. **The README still says the backfill adds three fields and lists three in the runner row** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:76` -- The backfill now writes `offeredAs` as a fourth attribution field (`command-offer.mjs:496`, `run-command-behaviour.mjs:824`), and the output sentence at `:188` names it, but the paragraph at `:76` still says \"adds those three fields\" and the `run-command-behaviour.mjs` row at `:125` still says `--backfill` rewrites with `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy` and `briefDelivered`. A reader following the section learns a three-field contract that the code no longer has. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:76]\n43:    Finding class: doc_code_drift\n44:    Scope proof: the README is in the declared accuracy-runner scope; the two code lines are the changed writers, and phase 027 T012 claims the README field lists.\n45:    Affected surface hints: README backfill section, runner table row, the `offeredAs` attribution contract.\n46:    Case: run `node .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs --backfill in.jsonl --out out.jsonl`; every output line carries `offeredAs` (pinned by `command-offer.vitest.ts:385-388`), while `README.md:76` says three fields and `:125` names only three.\n47: \n48: 2. **The README says every run line carries four attribution fields, but a head-moved line carries none** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:65` -- `runTurn` appends the head-moved line before the offer replay at `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1180-1184`, so that line has no `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs` or `briefDelivered`. The blanket sentence is false for the exit-3 path the README itself documents. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:65]\n49:    Finding class: doc_code_drift\n50:    Scope proof: the README and `run-command-behaviour.mjs` are both in the declared scope; the early append is the same writer's own branch.\n51:    Affected surface hints: head-moved run line, exit 3, attribution contract, scorer's `offerFieldAbsent`.\n52:    Case: a turn that commits or stashes during the run sets `headMoved`; `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1183` appends `{ ...line, restored: false, headMoved: true }` and returns exit 3. The written JSON has none of the four fields, while `README.md:65` says each appended line carries them. A scorer reading that line sees `offerFieldAbsent` even though the run line is valid.\n53: \n54: The A11 malformed-router row added at\n55: `doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt:268` agrees with the code: the doctor check reports\n56: `malformed <kind> row at line N: C cells where the header has H`\n57: (`agents-md-check.cjs:776-778`), and the embed only splices missing rows into the table\n58: (`agents-md-embed.cjs:373-410`), so the advice to fix the row by hand matches what embed will\n59: and will not do. No finding.\n60: \n61: ## Traceability Checks\n62: \n63: - `spec_code` -- partial. Phase 027 T006, T007, T010, T012, T013 and T017 are marked `[x]` with\n64:   evidence, and the code matches T006/T007/T010. T012's \"both field lists\" is narrower than the\n65:   README's actual field lists: the backfill paragraph and the runner table row still say three\n66:   fields.\n67: - `checklist_evidence` -- partial. `CHK-040` (tasks.md:244) asks `RA` to name `offeredAs` in both\n68:   field lists; the two lists T012 edited are correct, but the backfill lists are the remaining\n69:   drift. `CHK-FIX-003` and `CHK-FIX-004` remain open with the phase.\n70: - `feature_catalog_code` -- notApplicable. No feature-catalog page describes the two changed\n71:   writers; the routing-accuracy README is the shared doc.\n72: - `agent_cross_runtime` -- notApplicable. No runtime branch in the changed docs or writers.\n73: - `skill_agent` -- notApplicable. No agent definition changed.\n74: - `playbook_capability` -- notApplicable. No playbook surface changed.\n75: \n76: ## Integration Evidence\n77: \n78: - The routing-accuracy README is the only shared doc that describes `command-offer.mjs` and\n79:   `run-command-behaviour.mjs`; phase 027 T012 and T013 edit it as the doc of record.\n80: - The doctor presentation asset is the `/doctor:agents-md` troubleshooting text. Its new row\n81:   points at the same two scripts the doctor check and embed run:\n82:   `agents-md-check.cjs:757-808` and `agents-md-embed.cjs:782-803`.\n83: - The head-moved branch is the same `runTurn` function that now spreads `offerLineFields`; the\n84:   early return at `:1180-1184` is the one path that never reaches the offer replay.\n85: \n86: ## Edge Cases\n87: \n88: - A malformed shipped router row makes the checker report it as malformed and as missing. The\n89:   embed then adds a second, well-formed copy of that shipped row, and the malformed row stays.\n90:   The added A11 advice does not warn about the duplicate; the row still says embed never rewrites\n91:   a row, which is true, and the operator is told to fix the row by hand. Recorded as an operator\n92:   note, not a finding, because the added text does not claim the duplicate cannot happen.\n93: - The backfill's `--brief-only` path leaves a legacy line without `offeredAs`, which the README's\n94:   `--brief-only` paragraph already covers. The stale \"three fields\" paragraph is about the\n95:   default path, so the two statements do not conflict.\n96: - A head-moved line is written before `restoreTurn`, so `leftoverPaths` is absent too. The\n97:   README's head-moved paragraph names only `restored` and the changed paths; this is consistent\n98:   with the line and part of the same all-or-nothing early return.\n99: \n100: ## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n101: \n102: - The A11 malformed-row guidance matches the checker's message and the embed's insert-only\n103:   behavior.\n104: - The top attribution list (`README.md:65-70`) now names four fields, including `offeredAs`.\n105: - The output sentence (`README.md:188`) names `offeredAs` alongside the other backfill fields.\n106: - Phase 027 task rows T006, T007, T010, T012, T013 and T017 are marked `[x]` with evidence that\n107:   matches the changed lines this lineage read.\n108: \n109: ## Ruled Out\n110: \n111: - **The A11 row contradicts the doctor check.** Ruled out: the checker's malformed message names\n112:   the cell count and the header width, and the embed only adds missing rows.\n113: - **The top attribution list still says three fields.** Ruled out: `README.md:65` says four and\n114:   the item at `:69` defines `offeredAs`.\n115: - **The output-log sentence still omits `offeredAs`.** Ruled out: `README.md:188` lists it.\n116: - **The backfill paragraph's \"three fields\" is correct for `--brief-only`.** Ruled out: the\n117:   paragraph introduces the default backfill, and the separate `--brief-only` paragraph is the\n118:   one that describes copying offer fields untouched.\n119: \n120: ## Next Focus\n121: \n122: - Dimension: none remaining within the cap; synthesis\n123: - Focus area: compile the lineage report from the registry, the three deltas and the\n124:   documentation findings.\n125: - Reason: three iterations are complete, two clean code dimensions and two P2 doc drifts; the\n126:   cap is reached without a legal convergence stop.\n127: - Rotation status: correctness and security complete; traceability and maintainability covered by\n128:   the recovery pass (partial, because the packet's checklist is still open).\n129: - Required evidence: the registry's active counts, the three iteration final lines and the\n130:   synthesis report.\n131: - Blocked/productive carry-forward: no blocked approach.\n132: - Recovery note: the recovery pass changed granularity to line-level doc claims and produced the\n133:   two findings.\n134: \n135: ## Verdict\n136: \n137: No active P0 or P1 finding. Two P2 documentation drifts remain active; the verdict is PASS with\n138: advisories.\n139: \n140: Review verdict: PASS"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-4b/iterations/iteration-003.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794683641113,"end":1794683641498}}}}
