{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794683688083,"sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d3ffe8hgDLTRt6IhrOl","part":{"partID":"prt_1db7b74f0001dY2emxuCph3Stx","sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d3ffe8hgDLTRt6IhrOl","messageID":"msg_1db7b28780015k7Uv65qe4C0sc","type":"tool","id":"call_384feb9a327c4dfabba6bf0e","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 1\n\n- Mode: review\n- Lineage: `accuracy-runner-close-4c`\n- Run: `fanout-accuracy-runner-close-4c-1794682797954-pcdanq`\n- Iteration: 1 of 2\n- Dimension: correctness and security\n- Budget profile: verify (11-13 read actions)\n- Sources read: `review-brief-4c.txt`, `review-scope-4c.txt`, `review/verify-4/report.md`,\n  `027-review-pass-four-remediation/scratch/review-rounds.txt`, `028` task rows, the iteration-1\n  strategy, `steer.md` (absent)\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n`/deep:review` fan-out lineage `accuracy-runner-close-4c`. The closing round checks the 4c fix\nrange `48f03b5013..868b185e76` and the pass-four fixes this area's code already carries. The\nchanged accuracy-runner path in the scope file is the routing-accuracy `README.md`; the brief's\nchecks name the run-log writers, the transcript scorer, the Codex reader and the holdout guard as\nverification surfaces. The mention reader is the sibling lineage's surface and is read only as\ncontext.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:414-508`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:815-826,1170-1206`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:640-694,910-930`\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/codex.mjs:142-190`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:130-215`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:63-85,120-126,185-188`\n\nContext reads: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:373-380,422-439`\nand `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:158-179` for\nthe sibling or-list check; `027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:84-110` for the fix evidence.\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **A `2>` or `&>` redirect target that names a command document still counts as a start** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:677` -- `shellReadTargets` clears the candidate only when a word starts with `>`. `2>` and `&>` are redirect operators that do not start with `>`, so a target ending in `.md`, `.yaml` or `.yml` after either one is pushed as a read target. Since `readDocument` now treats a shell target that tails a command document as a start (`:922`), a reader command whose only relation to the document is a redirect is counted as a start. The brief's redirect check is therefore met for `>` but not for these two forms. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:677]\n   Finding class: correctness\n   Scope proof: `score-command-transcripts.mjs` is a named verification surface in the 4c brief; the shell branch at `:922` is the T009 fix this round checks, and `:677` is the redirect guard it relies on.\n   Affected surface hints: `startRate`, `startedOfOffered`, `loops`/`unsafe`, command documents, stderr redirects.\n   Case: `head -n 1 2> .skilled/commands/create/readme.md` followed by a `Write`; `shellReadTargets` returns the document path because `2>` is not recognized, `readDocument` returns true, and `startState.started` is true although the command read stdin and only wrote stderr to the document.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n- `spec_code` -- partial. Phase 027 T006, T007, T008, T009, T010, T011 and T030 are marked `[x]` with evidence. Reading the fixed files confirms the offeredAs writers, the heredoc end word, the shell-read start, the Codex resolved read and the live holdout guard. T009's redirect claim is only met for a bare `>`; `2>` and `&>` remain counted.\n- `checklist_evidence` -- partial. AC-003's four inputs (`cat`, `rg`, in-place `sed`, heredoc) read as the task describes, and `CHK-040`'s offeredAs claim is met by both writers. The brief's redirect input is not in AC-003's table, and the `2>` form is the remaining gap.\n- `skill_agent` -- notApplicable. No agent definition changed in this area.\n- `agent_cross_runtime` -- notApplicable. The Codex reader is a shared session reader, not an agent definition; its resolved-path read is checked directly.\n- `feature_catalog_code` -- notApplicable. No feature-catalog page describes the changed accuracy-runner lines.\n- `playbook_capability` -- notApplicable. No playbook surface changed.\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- The 4c brief's checks map to the fixed surfaces: T006/T007 (`command-offer.mjs:496`,\n  `run-command-behaviour.mjs:820-826,1203`), T008 (`score-command-transcripts.mjs:648`), T009\n  (`:916-929`), T010 (`codex.mjs:163-169`), T011\n  (`command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:134-149,201-210`) and T030 (`README.md:70,76,125`).\n- The shell branch at `:922` feeds `startState` and the loop readers, so the redirect edge reaches\n  `startRate`, `startedOfOffered` and the loop-safety counts, not only a diagnostic.\n- The sibling `scorer-attach-close-4c` lineage owns `command-attach.ts`. Reading the fixed\n  `COMMAND_OR_LIST` at `:380` and its three uses at `:427-439` shows a refusal, a question and a\n  request behave as the brief asks; no finding is raised against that surface here.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- `2>` and `&>` are recorded as the P2 finding above. A redirect placed before a real operand\n  (`cat > out.md prompts/x.md`) clears every later word, so a real read is missed; that is a false\n  negative and no current start figure depends on it, so it is recorded as a parser limit rather\n  than a second finding.\n- A bare document name is resolved through the last `cd` in the same shell command. A path with a\n  quoted space is unquoted before the `.md` test, so a quoted bare name is still matched; an\n  unquoted name with a space is not a valid one-word target.\n- Nested heredocs are not modeled. The pattern closes the first matching end word, which is the\n  shell's own rule for the opening delimiter; the T008 cases cover a hyphen and a dot end word.\n- The head-moved line intentionally carries none of the four attribution fields\n  (`run-command-behaviour.mjs:1180-1184`). `README.md:70` now states that exception, so\n  AR4B-P2-002 is confirmed fixed rather than re-reported.\n- The Codex reader keeps `recordedSessionId(lines, transcriptPath)` on the caller's locator while\n  reading `storePath`. The T010 test pins the link case; no new input was found that mismatches the\n  recorded id.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- Both run-log writers keep `offeredAs`: `command-offer.mjs:496` and\n  `run-command-behaviour.mjs:820-826,1203`.\n- A heredoc end word with a hyphen or a dot closes: `score-command-transcripts.mjs:648` accepts\n  `[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_.-]*` and matches the same text as the end word.\n- A search and an in-place `sed` are excluded: `:671` limits readers to `SHELL_READERS`, and `:673`\n  drops a `sed` with `--in-place`, `--in-place=`, or a clustered `-i` flag.\n- The Codex reader opens the containment-resolved file: `codex.mjs:163-169`.\n- The holdout guard reads the live capture: `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:201-210` checks\n  `publishedHoldoutIds(live, holdoutIds)` as well as the committed baseline.\n- The two 4b accuracy-runner findings are fixed: `README.md:76` says four fields, `:125` lists\n  `offeredAs`, and `:70` names the head-moved line's four-field exception.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **`offeredAs` is still dropped by a writer.** Ruled out: the backfill writes it at\n  `command-offer.mjs:496`, the live turn spreads it at `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1203`, and the\n  brief-only branch copies the input line's fields unchanged.\n- **A hyphen or dot heredoc end word is read as a command.** Ruled out:\n  `score-command-transcripts.mjs:648` captures the end word with `[A-Za-z0-9_.-]*`.\n- **The Codex reader still opens the caller's link.** Ruled out: `codex.mjs:169` reads\n  `storePath`, the path containment resolved.\n- **The holdout guard still checks only the committed baseline.** Ruled out:\n  `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:206-210` checks the live capture too.\n- **A refusal or question over an or-list carries a command.** Ruled out in the sibling area by\n  `command-attach.ts:380,427-439`; this lineage raises no finding against it.\n- **A stored run line can never carry `offeredAs`.** Not ruled out as a doc statement; it is the\n  iteration-2 traceability check, where the README sentence at `:123` is read against the fixed\n  writers.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: traceability and maintainability\n- Focus area: the routing-accuracy README sentences that describe `offeredAs`, the backfill\n  fields and the `--brief-only` path, including the T030 edits at `:70`, `:76` and `:125`\n- Reason: the code-side checks are confirmed; the remaining risk is a doc sentence that the\n  offeredAs writers made false\n- Rotation status: correctness and security complete; traceability and maintainability next\n- Required evidence: `README.md:63-85,120-126,185-188`, `command-offer.mjs:440-508`,\n  `run-command-behaviour.mjs:815-826,1187-1206`\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: the redirect parser edge is carried as a P2, not re-opened as\n  a code change\n- Recovery note: none\n\n## Verdict\n\nNo active P0 or P1 finding. One P2 correctness edge remains active; the verdict is PASS with\nadvisories.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-close-4c/iterations/iteration-001.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-close-4c/iterations/iteration-001.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-close-4c/iterations/iteration-001.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 1\\n\\n- Mode: review\\n- Lineage: `accuracy-runner-close-4c`\\n- Run: `fanout-accuracy-runner-close-4c-1794682797954-pcdanq`\\n- Iteration: 1 of 2\\n- Dimension: correctness and security\\n- Budget profile: verify (11-13 read actions)\\n- Sources read: `review-brief-4c.txt`, `review-scope-4c.txt`, `review/verify-4/report.md`,\\n  `027-review-pass-four-remediation/scratch/review-rounds.txt`, `028` task rows, the iteration-1\\n  strategy, `steer.md` (absent)\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n`/deep:review` fan-out lineage `accuracy-runner-close-4c`. The closing round checks the 4c fix\\nrange `48f03b5013..868b185e76` and the pass-four fixes this area's code already carries. The\\nchanged accuracy-runner path in the scope file is the routing-accuracy `README.md`; the brief's\\nchecks name the run-log writers, the transcript scorer, the Codex reader and the holdout guard as\\nverification surfaces. The mention reader is the sibling lineage's surface and is read only as\\ncontext.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:414-508`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:815-826,1170-1206`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:640-694,910-930`\\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/codex.mjs:142-190`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:130-215`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:63-85,120-126,185-188`\\n\\nContext reads: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:373-380,422-439`\\nand `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:158-179` for\\nthe sibling or-list check; `027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:84-110` for the fix evidence.\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **A `2>` or `&>` redirect target that names a command document still counts as a start** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:677` -- `shellReadTargets` clears the candidate only when a word starts with `>`. `2>` and `&>` are redirect operators that do not start with `>`, so a target ending in `.md`, `.yaml` or `.yml` after either one is pushed as a read target. Since `readDocument` now treats a shell target that tails a command document as a start (`:922`), a reader command whose only relation to the document is a redirect is counted as a start. The brief's redirect check is therefore met for `>` but not for these two forms. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:677]\\n   Finding class: correctness\\n   Scope proof: `score-command-transcripts.mjs` is a named verification surface in the 4c brief; the shell branch at `:922` is the T009 fix this round checks, and `:677` is the redirect guard it relies on.\\n   Affected surface hints: `startRate`, `startedOfOffered`, `loops`/`unsafe`, command documents, stderr redirects.\\n   Case: `head -n 1 2> .skilled/commands/create/readme.md` followed by a `Write`; `shellReadTargets` returns the document path because `2>` is not recognized, `readDocument` returns true, and `startState.started` is true although the command read stdin and only wrote stderr to the document.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n- `spec_code` -- partial. Phase 027 T006, T007, T008, T009, T010, T011 and T030 are marked `[x]` with evidence. Reading the fixed files confirms the offeredAs writers, the heredoc end word, the shell-read start, the Codex resolved read and the live holdout guard. T009's redirect claim is only met for a bare `>`; `2>` and `&>` remain counted.\\n- `checklist_evidence` -- partial. AC-003's four inputs (`cat`, `rg`, in-place `sed`, heredoc) read as the task describes, and `CHK-040`'s offeredAs claim is met by both writers. The brief's redirect input is not in AC-003's table, and the `2>` form is the remaining gap.\\n- `skill_agent` -- notApplicable. No agent definition changed in this area.\\n- `agent_cross_runtime` -- notApplicable. The Codex reader is a shared session reader, not an agent definition; its resolved-path read is checked directly.\\n- `feature_catalog_code` -- notApplicable. No feature-catalog page describes the changed accuracy-runner lines.\\n- `playbook_capability` -- notApplicable. No playbook surface changed.\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- The 4c brief's checks map to the fixed surfaces: T006/T007 (`command-offer.mjs:496`,\\n  `run-command-behaviour.mjs:820-826,1203`), T008 (`score-command-transcripts.mjs:648`), T009\\n  (`:916-929`), T010 (`codex.mjs:163-169`), T011\\n  (`command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:134-149,201-210`) and T030 (`README.md:70,76,125`).\\n- The shell branch at `:922` feeds `startState` and the loop readers, so the redirect edge reaches\\n  `startRate`, `startedOfOffered` and the loop-safety counts, not only a diagnostic.\\n- The sibling `scorer-attach-close-4c` lineage owns `command-attach.ts`. Reading the fixed\\n  `COMMAND_OR_LIST` at `:380` and its three uses at `:427-439` shows a refusal, a question and a\\n  request behave as the brief asks; no finding is raised against that surface here.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- `2>` and `&>` are recorded as the P2 finding above. A redirect placed before a real operand\\n  (`cat > out.md prompts/x.md`) clears every later word, so a real read is missed; that is a false\\n  negative and no current start figure depends on it, so it is recorded as a parser limit rather\\n  than a second finding.\\n- A bare document name is resolved through the last `cd` in the same shell command. A path with a\\n  quoted space is unquoted before the `.md` test, so a quoted bare name is still matched; an\\n  unquoted name with a space is not a valid one-word target.\\n- Nested heredocs are not modeled. The pattern closes the first matching end word, which is the\\n  shell's own rule for the opening delimiter; the T008 cases cover a hyphen and a dot end word.\\n- The head-moved line intentionally carries none of the four attribution fields\\n  (`run-command-behaviour.mjs:1180-1184`). `README.md:70` now states that exception, so\\n  AR4B-P2-002 is confirmed fixed rather than re-reported.\\n- The Codex reader keeps `recordedSessionId(lines, transcriptPath)` on the caller's locator while\\n  reading `storePath`. The T010 test pins the link case; no new input was found that mismatches the\\n  recorded id.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- Both run-log writers keep `offeredAs`: `command-offer.mjs:496` and\\n  `run-command-behaviour.mjs:820-826,1203`.\\n- A heredoc end word with a hyphen or a dot closes: `score-command-transcripts.mjs:648` accepts\\n  `[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_.-]*` and matches the same text as the end word.\\n- A search and an in-place `sed` are excluded: `:671` limits readers to `SHELL_READERS`, and `:673`\\n  drops a `sed` with `--in-place`, `--in-place=`, or a clustered `-i` flag.\\n- The Codex reader opens the containment-resolved file: `codex.mjs:163-169`.\\n- The holdout guard reads the live capture: `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:201-210` checks\\n  `publishedHoldoutIds(live, holdoutIds)` as well as the committed baseline.\\n- The two 4b accuracy-runner findings are fixed: `README.md:76` says four fields, `:125` lists\\n  `offeredAs`, and `:70` names the head-moved line's four-field exception.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **`offeredAs` is still dropped by a writer.** Ruled out: the backfill writes it at\\n  `command-offer.mjs:496`, the live turn spreads it at `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1203`, and the\\n  brief-only branch copies the input line's fields unchanged.\\n- **A hyphen or dot heredoc end word is read as a command.** Ruled out:\\n  `score-command-transcripts.mjs:648` captures the end word with `[A-Za-z0-9_.-]*`.\\n- **The Codex reader still opens the caller's link.** Ruled out: `codex.mjs:169` reads\\n  `storePath`, the path containment resolved.\\n- **The holdout guard still checks only the committed baseline.** Ruled out:\\n  `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:206-210` checks the live capture too.\\n- **A refusal or question over an or-list carries a command.** Ruled out in the sibling area by\\n  `command-attach.ts:380,427-439`; this lineage raises no finding against it.\\n- **A stored run line can never carry `offeredAs`.** Not ruled out as a doc statement; it is the\\n  iteration-2 traceability check, where the README sentence at `:123` is read against the fixed\\n  writers.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: traceability and maintainability\\n- Focus area: the routing-accuracy README sentences that describe `offeredAs`, the backfill\\n  fields and the `--brief-only` path, including the T030 edits at `:70`, `:76` and `:125`\\n- Reason: the code-side checks are confirmed; the remaining risk is a doc sentence that the\\n  offeredAs writers made false\\n- Rotation status: correctness and security complete; traceability and maintainability next\\n- Required evidence: `README.md:63-85,120-126,185-188`, `command-offer.mjs:440-508`,\\n  `run-command-behaviour.mjs:815-826,1187-1206`\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: the redirect parser edge is carried as a P2, not re-opened as\\n  a code change\\n- Recovery note: none\\n\\n## Verdict\\n\\nNo active P0 or P1 finding. One P2 correctness edge remains active; the verdict is PASS with\\nadvisories.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-close-4c/iterations/iteration-001.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794683663600,"end":1794683688083}}}}
