{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794683937633,"sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d3ffe8hgDLTRt6IhrOl","part":{"partID":"prt_1db7f3e4c002LFvV2ZWo3xiSS8","sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d3ffe8hgDLTRt6IhrOl","messageID":"msg_1db7ee892001u2M0uOT0oX1vyI","type":"tool","id":"call_c0045d3dea4f4abd97f31970","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 2\n\n- Mode: review\n- Lineage: `accuracy-runner-close-4c`\n- Run: `fanout-accuracy-runner-close-4c-1794682797954-pcdanq`\n- Iteration: 2 of 2\n- Dimension: traceability and maintainability\n- Budget profile: adjudicate (8-10 read actions)\n- Sources read: `review-brief-4c.txt`, `steer.md` (absent), the iteration-1 strategy and registry,\n  `review/verify-4/report.md`, `027-review-pass-four-remediation/scratch/review-rounds.txt`,\n  `027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md:204-238`, `tasks.md:100-110`\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n`/deep:review` fan-out lineage `accuracy-runner-close-4c`. The traceability pass reads the\nrouting-accuracy `README.md` against the writers and the scorer after the 4c doc fix. It confirms\nthe two 4b accuracy-runner findings and looks for sentences the `offeredAs` persistence fix made\nfalse.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:63-85,120-126,185-188`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:440-508`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:980-1085,1187-1206`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1458-1478,1620-1685,1880-1897`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md:204-238`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:100-110`\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **The README says a stored run line holds no `offeredAs`, but both current writers store it** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:123` -- The sentence \"A stored run line holds no `offeredAs`, so its offer counts as before\" is now true only for a line written before the field existed. The backfill writes `offeredAs` at `command-offer.mjs:496`, the live turn spreads `offerLineFields` at `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1203`, and the scorer reads it at `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1471-1476` to split `offeredAsPartner` from `offered`. A newly stored line therefore holds the field, and a partner-side command is counted in `offeredAsPartner`, not in `offered`. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:123]\n   Finding class: traceability\n   Scope proof: the README is the changed accuracy-runner path in `review-scope-4c.txt`; both writers and the scorer are the brief's verification surfaces.\n   Affected surface hints: `offerOf`, `offeredAsPartner`, `offerFieldAbsent`, stored run logs, backfill.\n   Case: a live line written at `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1201-1205` carries `offeredAs: \"partner\"`; `offerOf` counts it in `offeredAsPartner` and not in `offered`, while `README.md:123` says a stored line holds no `offeredAs` and counts as before.\n   Claim: the blanket stored-line statement is false after the writers began keeping `offeredAs`.\n   Evidence refs: `README.md:123`, `command-offer.mjs:496`, `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1203`, `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1471-1476`.\n   Counterevidence sought: checked whether `stored` is defined elsewhere as a pre-field line; the README's `--brief-only` paragraph at `:85` says \"present or absent\", so the document already knows a stored line can hold the field.\n   Alternative explanation: the sentence was written when only legacy lines existed and was not updated after T006/T007.\n   Final severity: P2. Confidence: high.\n   Downgrade trigger: withdraw if a later definition names `stored` as the pre-offeredAs corpus only.\n\n2. **The runner row says `--brief-only` rewrites the four fields, but that mode copies the offer fields untouched** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:125` -- The row lists `[--brief-only]` in the same sentence as \"rewrites a finished log with `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs` and `briefDelivered`\". `backfillRunLog` at `command-offer.mjs:489-490` copies the line and changes only `briefDelivered` and `briefBackfilled` when `briefOnly`; a legacy line with no offer fields stays without them. The paragraph at `README.md:85` already says brief-only keeps every offer field exactly as the input line holds it. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:125]\n   Finding class: maintainability\n   Scope proof: the README is the changed accuracy-runner path; the backfill branch is the writer the row describes.\n   Affected surface hints: `--brief-only`, backfill field list, `briefBackfilled`, legacy run logs.\n   Case: a legacy line with no `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy` or `offeredAs`, run through `--backfill --brief-only`; the output line has `briefDelivered` and `briefBackfilled` but none of the three offer fields, contradicting the runner row.\n   Claim: the `[--brief-only]` clause in the row promises the four-field rewrite the mode does not perform.\n   Evidence refs: `README.md:125`, `README.md:85`, `command-offer.mjs:489-490`, `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1067-1082`.\n   Counterevidence sought: checked whether `--brief-only` is rejected with `--backfill` or whether the row scopes the bracket to a different path; `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1081-1082` accepts the pair, and the row names both in one sentence.\n   Alternative explanation: \"rewrites with\" could mean the output may hold the fields when the input does; the paragraph at `:85` is the precise statement, and the row is the imprecise one.\n   Final severity: P2. Confidence: high.\n   Downgrade trigger: withdraw if the row is read as describing the default backfill only and the bracket is treated as a separate mode heading.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n- `spec_code` -- partial. T030 fixed the two 4b list counts and added the head-moved sentence; `README.md:70` matches `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1180-1184`, `:76` says four fields and `:125` lists `offeredAs`. The two sentences above remain the only doc-code drift.\n- `checklist_evidence` -- partial. AC-010 asks the docs to name the behaviour the code has; the T030 sentences do, but `:123` and the `[--brief-only]` clause at `:125` do not. `CHK-040`'s offeredAs field-list claim is met by both lists.\n- `skill_agent` -- notApplicable. No agent definition changed in this area.\n- `agent_cross_runtime` -- notApplicable. No runtime branch in the changed doc; the Codex reader is covered by the iteration-1 check.\n- `feature_catalog_code` -- notApplicable. No feature-catalog page describes the changed accuracy-runner lines.\n- `playbook_capability` -- notApplicable. No playbook surface changed.\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- The 4c brief's \"docs agree with code\" check is the one this pass runs. Its doc of record is\n  `routing-accuracy/README.md`; the code it describes is `command-offer.mjs`,\n  `run-command-behaviour.mjs` and `score-command-transcripts.mjs`.\n- The T030 verification strings are present: `rg 'three fields'` finds nothing,\n  `README.md:70` carries \"carries none of the four\", and `README.md:125` carries the four-field\n  backfill list.\n- The verify-4 report's deferred items are phase 026 work by\n  `027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md:214`: the pair-doc shared-row sentence, the reserved\n  `paired` arm name and the `unscoredOnly` field are not re-reported here.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- The `--brief-only` sentence at `:125` and the paragraph at `:85` contradict each other. The\n  finding cites the row because T030 edited it; the paragraph is the correct statement and needs\n  no change.\n- The stored-line sentence at `:123` can be read as the legacy corpus the scorer was built on.\n  The finding is scoped to a line written by the current writers, which the T006/T007 fix makes\n  possible; it does not dispute a legacy line's count.\n- The pair-doc shared-row sentence (`:123`), the reserved `paired` arm name and the dead\n  `unscoredOnly` field remain open by design. They are deferred to phase 026 and are not counted\n  as new findings.\n- The redirect P2 from iteration 1 remains active. It is carried forward, not re-opened as a\n  second finding.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- AR4B-P2-001 is fixed: `README.md:76` says \"four fields\", `:125` lists `offeredAs` in the backfill\n  field list, and no \"three fields\" string remains in the document.\n- AR4B-P2-002 is fixed: `README.md:70` names the head-moved line's four-field exception, and the\n  exception matches `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1180-1184`.\n- The backfill's default path writes the four attribution fields plus `offerError` and\n  `offerBackfilled` (`command-offer.mjs:492-500`), and `README.md:188` lists them.\n- The brief-only path copies a present offer and leaves an absent one absent\n  (`command-offer.mjs:489-490`), as `README.md:85` says.\n- The head-moved row says `restored: false` and lists the changed paths\n  (`run-command-behaviour.mjs:1183-1184`), as `README.md:125` says.\n- The `--pair` block's shape (`from`, `to`, `rows`, `gained`, `lost`, `bothFollowed`,\n  `neitherFollowed`) matches `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1896`; the shared-owned-row limit is\n  the deferred phase 026 item, not a new finding.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **The T030 edits are incomplete.** Ruled out: the three exact strings are present, and the\n  head-moved sentence matches the writer's early return.\n- **The top field list still says three fields.** Ruled out: `README.md:65-70` names four,\n  including `offeredAs` and the head-moved exception.\n- **The output sentence still omits `offeredAs`.** Ruled out: `README.md:188` lists it.\n- **The pair-doc shared-row limit is a new finding.** Ruled out: `027` spec:214 defers the pair\n  doc, the `paired` name and `unscoredOnly` to phase 026.\n- **The redirect edge is a P1.** Ruled out: the false start needs a `2>` or `&>` target that names\n  a command document, and the parser's supported redirect grammar is a P2 edge, not a blocked\n  release path.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: none remaining within the cap; synthesis\n- Focus area: compile the lineage report from the registry, the two deltas and the three active\n  P2 findings.\n- Reason: two iterations are complete; the cap is reached with three active P2 advisories and no\n  P0/P1.\n- Rotation status: correctness and security complete in iteration 1; traceability and\n  maintainability complete in iteration 2.\n- Required evidence: the registry's active counts, the two iteration final lines and the synthesis\n  report.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: no blocked approach; the redirect P2 is carried.\n- Recovery note: none; the cap is reached before a legal convergence stop.\n\n## Verdict\n\nNo active P0 or P1 finding. Three P2 documentation and parser-edge findings remain active; the\nverdict is PASS with advisories.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-close-4c/iterations/iteration-002.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-close-4c/iterations/iteration-002.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-close-4c/iterations/iteration-002.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 2\\n\\n- Mode: review\\n- Lineage: `accuracy-runner-close-4c`\\n- Run: `fanout-accuracy-runner-close-4c-1794682797954-pcdanq`\\n- Iteration: 2 of 2\\n- Dimension: traceability and maintainability\\n- Budget profile: adjudicate (8-10 read actions)\\n- Sources read: `review-brief-4c.txt`, `steer.md` (absent), the iteration-1 strategy and registry,\\n  `review/verify-4/report.md`, `027-review-pass-four-remediation/scratch/review-rounds.txt`,\\n  `027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md:204-238`, `tasks.md:100-110`\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n`/deep:review` fan-out lineage `accuracy-runner-close-4c`. The traceability pass reads the\\nrouting-accuracy `README.md` against the writers and the scorer after the 4c doc fix. It confirms\\nthe two 4b accuracy-runner findings and looks for sentences the `offeredAs` persistence fix made\\nfalse.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:63-85,120-126,185-188`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:440-508`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:980-1085,1187-1206`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1458-1478,1620-1685,1880-1897`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md:204-238`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:100-110`\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **The README says a stored run line holds no `offeredAs`, but both current writers store it** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:123` -- The sentence \\\"A stored run line holds no `offeredAs`, so its offer counts as before\\\" is now true only for a line written before the field existed. The backfill writes `offeredAs` at `command-offer.mjs:496`, the live turn spreads `offerLineFields` at `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1203`, and the scorer reads it at `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1471-1476` to split `offeredAsPartner` from `offered`. A newly stored line therefore holds the field, and a partner-side command is counted in `offeredAsPartner`, not in `offered`. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:123]\\n   Finding class: traceability\\n   Scope proof: the README is the changed accuracy-runner path in `review-scope-4c.txt`; both writers and the scorer are the brief's verification surfaces.\\n   Affected surface hints: `offerOf`, `offeredAsPartner`, `offerFieldAbsent`, stored run logs, backfill.\\n   Case: a live line written at `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1201-1205` carries `offeredAs: \\\"partner\\\"`; `offerOf` counts it in `offeredAsPartner` and not in `offered`, while `README.md:123` says a stored line holds no `offeredAs` and counts as before.\\n   Claim: the blanket stored-line statement is false after the writers began keeping `offeredAs`.\\n   Evidence refs: `README.md:123`, `command-offer.mjs:496`, `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1203`, `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1471-1476`.\\n   Counterevidence sought: checked whether `stored` is defined elsewhere as a pre-field line; the README's `--brief-only` paragraph at `:85` says \\\"present or absent\\\", so the document already knows a stored line can hold the field.\\n   Alternative explanation: the sentence was written when only legacy lines existed and was not updated after T006/T007.\\n   Final severity: P2. Confidence: high.\\n   Downgrade trigger: withdraw if a later definition names `stored` as the pre-offeredAs corpus only.\\n\\n2. **The runner row says `--brief-only` rewrites the four fields, but that mode copies the offer fields untouched** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:125` -- The row lists `[--brief-only]` in the same sentence as \\\"rewrites a finished log with `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs` and `briefDelivered`\\\". `backfillRunLog` at `command-offer.mjs:489-490` copies the line and changes only `briefDelivered` and `briefBackfilled` when `briefOnly`; a legacy line with no offer fields stays without them. The paragraph at `README.md:85` already says brief-only keeps every offer field exactly as the input line holds it. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:125]\\n   Finding class: maintainability\\n   Scope proof: the README is the changed accuracy-runner path; the backfill branch is the writer the row describes.\\n   Affected surface hints: `--brief-only`, backfill field list, `briefBackfilled`, legacy run logs.\\n   Case: a legacy line with no `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy` or `offeredAs`, run through `--backfill --brief-only`; the output line has `briefDelivered` and `briefBackfilled` but none of the three offer fields, contradicting the runner row.\\n   Claim: the `[--brief-only]` clause in the row promises the four-field rewrite the mode does not perform.\\n   Evidence refs: `README.md:125`, `README.md:85`, `command-offer.mjs:489-490`, `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1067-1082`.\\n   Counterevidence sought: checked whether `--brief-only` is rejected with `--backfill` or whether the row scopes the bracket to a different path; `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1081-1082` accepts the pair, and the row names both in one sentence.\\n   Alternative explanation: \\\"rewrites with\\\" could mean the output may hold the fields when the input does; the paragraph at `:85` is the precise statement, and the row is the imprecise one.\\n   Final severity: P2. Confidence: high.\\n   Downgrade trigger: withdraw if the row is read as describing the default backfill only and the bracket is treated as a separate mode heading.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n- `spec_code` -- partial. T030 fixed the two 4b list counts and added the head-moved sentence; `README.md:70` matches `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1180-1184`, `:76` says four fields and `:125` lists `offeredAs`. The two sentences above remain the only doc-code drift.\\n- `checklist_evidence` -- partial. AC-010 asks the docs to name the behaviour the code has; the T030 sentences do, but `:123` and the `[--brief-only]` clause at `:125` do not. `CHK-040`'s offeredAs field-list claim is met by both lists.\\n- `skill_agent` -- notApplicable. No agent definition changed in this area.\\n- `agent_cross_runtime` -- notApplicable. No runtime branch in the changed doc; the Codex reader is covered by the iteration-1 check.\\n- `feature_catalog_code` -- notApplicable. No feature-catalog page describes the changed accuracy-runner lines.\\n- `playbook_capability` -- notApplicable. No playbook surface changed.\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- The 4c brief's \\\"docs agree with code\\\" check is the one this pass runs. Its doc of record is\\n  `routing-accuracy/README.md`; the code it describes is `command-offer.mjs`,\\n  `run-command-behaviour.mjs` and `score-command-transcripts.mjs`.\\n- The T030 verification strings are present: `rg 'three fields'` finds nothing,\\n  `README.md:70` carries \\\"carries none of the four\\\", and `README.md:125` carries the four-field\\n  backfill list.\\n- The verify-4 report's deferred items are phase 026 work by\\n  `027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md:214`: the pair-doc shared-row sentence, the reserved\\n  `paired` arm name and the `unscoredOnly` field are not re-reported here.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- The `--brief-only` sentence at `:125` and the paragraph at `:85` contradict each other. The\\n  finding cites the row because T030 edited it; the paragraph is the correct statement and needs\\n  no change.\\n- The stored-line sentence at `:123` can be read as the legacy corpus the scorer was built on.\\n  The finding is scoped to a line written by the current writers, which the T006/T007 fix makes\\n  possible; it does not dispute a legacy line's count.\\n- The pair-doc shared-row sentence (`:123`), the reserved `paired` arm name and the dead\\n  `unscoredOnly` field remain open by design. They are deferred to phase 026 and are not counted\\n  as new findings.\\n- The redirect P2 from iteration 1 remains active. It is carried forward, not re-opened as a\\n  second finding.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- AR4B-P2-001 is fixed: `README.md:76` says \\\"four fields\\\", `:125` lists `offeredAs` in the backfill\\n  field list, and no \\\"three fields\\\" string remains in the document.\\n- AR4B-P2-002 is fixed: `README.md:70` names the head-moved line's four-field exception, and the\\n  exception matches `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1180-1184`.\\n- The backfill's default path writes the four attribution fields plus `offerError` and\\n  `offerBackfilled` (`command-offer.mjs:492-500`), and `README.md:188` lists them.\\n- The brief-only path copies a present offer and leaves an absent one absent\\n  (`command-offer.mjs:489-490`), as `README.md:85` says.\\n- The head-moved row says `restored: false` and lists the changed paths\\n  (`run-command-behaviour.mjs:1183-1184`), as `README.md:125` says.\\n- The `--pair` block's shape (`from`, `to`, `rows`, `gained`, `lost`, `bothFollowed`,\\n  `neitherFollowed`) matches `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1896`; the shared-owned-row limit is\\n  the deferred phase 026 item, not a new finding.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **The T030 edits are incomplete.** Ruled out: the three exact strings are present, and the\\n  head-moved sentence matches the writer's early return.\\n- **The top field list still says three fields.** Ruled out: `README.md:65-70` names four,\\n  including `offeredAs` and the head-moved exception.\\n- **The output sentence still omits `offeredAs`.** Ruled out: `README.md:188` lists it.\\n- **The pair-doc shared-row limit is a new finding.** Ruled out: `027` spec:214 defers the pair\\n  doc, the `paired` name and `unscoredOnly` to phase 026.\\n- **The redirect edge is a P1.** Ruled out: the false start needs a `2>` or `&>` target that names\\n  a command document, and the parser's supported redirect grammar is a P2 edge, not a blocked\\n  release path.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: none remaining within the cap; synthesis\\n- Focus area: compile the lineage report from the registry, the two deltas and the three active\\n  P2 findings.\\n- Reason: two iterations are complete; the cap is reached with three active P2 advisories and no\\n  P0/P1.\\n- Rotation status: correctness and security complete in iteration 1; traceability and\\n  maintainability complete in iteration 2.\\n- Required evidence: the registry's active counts, the two iteration final lines and the synthesis\\n  report.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: no blocked approach; the redirect P2 is carried.\\n- Recovery note: none; the cap is reached before a legal convergence stop.\\n\\n## Verdict\\n\\nNo active P0 or P1 finding. Three P2 documentation and parser-edge findings remain active; the\\nverdict is PASS with advisories.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-close-4c/iterations/iteration-002.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794683911756,"end":1794683937633}}}}
