ls/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:123\",\n      \"line\": 123,\n      \"dimension\": \"traceability\",\n      \"findingClass\": \"traceability\",\n      \"evidenceRefs\": [\n        \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:123\",\n        \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:496\",\n        \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:1203\",\n        \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1471-1476\"\n      ],\n      \"claim\": \"The blanket sentence 'A stored run line holds no offeredAs, so its offer counts as before' is false for a line written by either current writer, because both writers keep the field and the scorer uses it to split partner from head.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command-offer.mjs:496 writes offeredAs on a backfilled line; run-command-behaviour.mjs:1203 spreads offerLineFields, which writes it at :824; score-command-transcripts.mjs:1471-1476 reads line.offeredAs.\",\n      \"counterevidenceSought\": \"Checked whether 'stored' is defined as the pre-field corpus only. The README's own --brief-only paragraph at :85 says a field may be present or absent, so the document already knows a stored line can hold it.\",\n      \"alternativeExplanation\": \"The sentence was written when only legacy lines existed and was not updated after T006/T007.\",\n      \"finalSeverity\": \"P2\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"downgradeTrigger\": \"Withdraw if a later definition names 'stored' as the pre-offeredAs corpus only.\",\n      \"case\": \"A live line written at run-command-behaviour.mjs:1201-1205 carries offeredAs 'partner'; offerOf counts it in offeredAsPartner and not in offered, while README.md:123 says a stored line holds no offeredAs and counts as before.\",\n      \"scopeProof\": \"The README is the changed accuracy-runner path in review-scope-4c.txt; both writers and the scorer are the brief's verification surfaces.\",\n      \"affectedSurfaceHints\": [\n        \"offerOf\",\n        \"offeredAsPartner\",\n        \"offerFieldAbsent\",\n        \"stored run logs\",\n        \"backfill\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ARC4C-P2-003\",\n      \"severity\": \"P2\",\n      \"title\": \"The runner row says --brief-only rewrites the four fields, but that mode copies the offer fields untouched\",\n      \"file\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:125\",\n      \"line\": 125,\n      \"dimension\": \"maintainability\",\n      \"findingClass\": \"maintainability\",\n      \"evidenceRefs\": [\n        \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:125\",\n        \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:85\",\n        \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:489-490\",\n        \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:1067-1082\"\n      ],\n      \"claim\": \"The runner row's [--brief-only] clause promises a four-field rewrite, but the brief-only branch copies the input line and changes only briefDelivered and briefBackfilled, so a legacy line keeps no offer fields.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command-offer.mjs:489-490 builds { ...line, briefDelivered, briefBackfilled } when briefOnly; the else branch at :492-500 writes the four offer fields. README.md:85 says brief-only keeps every offer field as the input holds it.\",\n      \"counterevidenceSought\": \"Checked whether --brief-only is rejected with --backfill or scoped differently in the run options; run-command-behaviour.mjs:1067-1082 accepts the pair, and the row names both in one sentence.\",\n      \"alternativeExplanation\": \"'Rewrites with' could mean the output may hold the fields when the input does; the paragraph at :85 is the precise statement, and the row is the imprecise one.\",\n      \"finalSeverity\": \"P2\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"downgradeTrigger\": \"Withdraw if the row is read as describing the default backfill only and the bracket is treated as a separate mode heading.\",\n      \"case\": \"A legacy line with no offeredCommand, offeredPolicy or offeredAs, run through --backfill --brief-only; the output has briefDelivered and briefBackfilled but none of the three offer fields, contradicting the runner row.\",\n      \"scopeProof\": \"The README is the changed accuracy-runner path; the backfill branch is the writer the row describes.\",\n      \"affectedSurfaceHints\": [\n        \"--brief-only\",\n        \"backfill field list\",\n        \"briefBackfilled\",\n        \"legacy run logs\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"traceabilityChecks\": {\n    \"spec_code\": {\n      \"level\": \"core\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"notes\": \"T030 fixed the two 4b list counts and added the head-moved sentence; README:70 matches run-command-behaviour.mjs:1180-1184, :76 says four fields and :125 lists offeredAs. The stored-line sentence at :123 and the [--brief-only] clause at :125 remain doc-code drift.\"\n    },\n    \"checklist_evidence\": {\n      \"level\": \"core\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"notes\": \"AC-010 asks the docs to name the behaviour the code has; the T030 sentences do, but :123 and the [--brief-only] clause at :125 do not. CHK-040's offeredAs field-list claim is met by both lists.\"\n    },\n    \"skill_agent\": {\n      \"level\": \"overlay\",\n      \"status\": \"notApplicable\",\n      \"notes\": \"No agent definition changed in this area.\"\n    },\n    \"agent_cross_runtime\": {\n      \"level\": \"overlay\",\n      \"status\": \"notApplicable\",\n      \"notes\": \"No runtime branch in the changed doc; the Codex reader is covered by the iteration-1 check.\"\n    },\n    \"feature_c