{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794684266396,"sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d3ffe8hgDLTRt6IhrOl","part":{"partID":"prt_1db840c67002iHRcCPWWbGTRti","sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d3ffe8hgDLTRt6IhrOl","messageID":"msg_1db83b62e001HPDT7f3imiHgXj","type":"tool","id":"call_a5233125ea42492ab6a20a0d","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Report: Command Surfacing Build, Pass Four (accuracy-runner closeout lineage)\n\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder)\n- Pass: the closing round of review pass four, on the fix range `48f03b5013..868b185e76`.\n- Lineage: `accuracy-runner-close-4c`, area `accuracy-runner`, run\n  `fanout-accuracy-runner-close-4c-1794682797954-pcdanq`, executor `cli-opencode`\n  `opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash` at reasoning effort max.\n- Reviewed scope: the one accuracy-runner path in `review/review-scope-4c.txt` (the routing-accuracy\n  `README.md`) plus the six code and test surfaces the brief names as verification checks: the two\n  run-log writers, the transcript scorer, the Codex reader and the holdout guard.\n- Inputs to this synthesis: the two iteration narratives, the two delta files, the lineage registry\n  (3 active P2 findings), the strategy and the dashboard.\n- Cross-area boundary: `lib/command-attach.ts`, the scorer fusion, the recommend handler and the\n  feature docs belong to `scorer-attach-close-4c`. This lineage read the mention reader only as\n  context and raises no finding against it.\n- Iteration cap: 2 of 2. The loop stopped at the cap; convergence was not declared.\n- Operator review focus: Closing round of review pass four of command surfacing. FIRST read and\n  follow `review-brief-4c.txt`; it names the scope file, the commit range, which files the lineage\n  reviews and the checks. HOLDOUT RULE: never open `command-prompts.jsonl` or\n  `holdout-prompts.jsonl` except through `jq 'del(.prompt)'`, never run `git diff`, `show` or\n  `log -p` over a path that includes `command-prompts.jsonl` without the pathspec\n  `:(exclude)**/command-prompts.jsonl`, and never print a prompt whose split is holdout. The\n  reviewer changes no code and writes only inside its lineage folder.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\n- **Finding verdict: PASS.** No P0 and no P1 finding is active.\n- **hasAdvisories: true.** Three P2 findings remain active: one parser edge and two documentation\n  drifts.\n- **Active counts:** P0 0, P1 0, P2 3.\n- **The 4b accuracy-runner P2s are fixed.** `README.md:76` now says four fields, `:125` lists\n  `offeredAs`, and `:70` names the head-moved line's four-field exception. No \"three fields\" string\n  remains.\n- **Both run-log writers keep `offeredAs`.** The backfill writes it at `command-offer.mjs:496`, the\n  live turn spreads `offerLineFields` at `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1203`, and the scorer reads it\n  at `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1471-1476`.\n- **The other brief checks hold.** A `cat` of a command document counts as a start; `rg`, an\n  in-place `sed` and a heredoc line do not. A heredoc end word with a hyphen or a dot closes. The\n  Codex reader opens `storePath`, the file containment resolved. The holdout guard checks the live\n  capture as well as the committed baseline.\n- **The new P2 parser edge.** `shellReadTargets` recognizes only a word starting with `>` as a\n  redirect, so a `2>` or `&>` target that names a command document is counted as a read and, through\n  `readDocument`, as a start (`score-command-transcripts.mjs:677,922`).\n- **The two new P2 doc drifts.** `README.md:123` still says a stored run line holds no `offeredAs`,\n  which the fixed writers made false. `README.md:125` puts `[--brief-only]` inside a sentence that\n  promises the four-field rewrite, which that mode does not perform; `README.md:85` states the\n  correct behavior.\n- **Search debt.** One deferred scope row records the phase 026 items (pair-doc shared row,\n  reserved `paired` arm name, dead `unscoredOnly` field). The dashboard's provisional verdict is\n  CONDITIONAL on that debt; the finding-severity verdict is PASS, and the cross-lineage merge\n  recomputes from the findings registry.\n- **Holdout hygiene:** no holdout prompt text was read or printed. Corpus access was limited to the\n  code and the committed test, and no prompt value is used in a finding or report sentence.\n- **Release readiness:** `in-progress`. The cap was reached; no convergence event was recorded.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Planning Trigger\n\nNo plan is required for the PASS finding verdict. The three P2s are advisory: two documentation\ncorrections and one small parser guard. They do not block release. The phase 026 deferral is\nrecorded as search debt, not as a new finding.\n\n```json Planning Packet\n{\n  \"triggered\": false,\n  \"triggerReason\": \"PASS with three advisory P2 findings; no P0 or P1 remains.\",\n  \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n  \"dashboardVerdict\": \"CONDITIONAL\",\n  \"hasAdvisories\": true,\n  \"hasSearchDebt\": true,\n  \"counts\": { \"p0\": 0, \"p1\": 0, \"p2\": 3, \"active\": 3, \"iterations\": 2 },\n  \"activeFindings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ARC4C-P2-001\",\n      \"severity\": \"P2\",\n      \"title\": \"A 2> or &> redirect target that names a command document still counts as a start\",\n      \"file\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:677\",\n      \"findingClass\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"advisory\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ARC4C-P2-002\",\n      \"severity\": \"P2\",\n      \"title\": \"The README says a stored run line holds no offeredAs, but both current writers store it\",\n      \"file\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:123\",\n      \"findingClass\": \"traceability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"advisory\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ARC4C-P2-003\",\n      \"severity\": \"P2\",\n      \"title\": \"The runner row says --brief-only rewrites the four fields, but that mode copies the offer fields untouched\",\n      \"file\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:125\",\n      \"findingClass\": \"maintainability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"advisory\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"remediationWorkstreams\": [\n    {\n      \"order\": 1,\n      \"advisory\": true,\n      \"name\": \"Redirect operator parsing\",\n      \"files\": [\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs\"],\n      \"actions\": [\n        \"Recognize 2>, &>, 2>> and &>> as redirect operators in shellReadTargets, not only a word starting with >.\",\n        \"Skip the redirect target rather than every later word, so a real read after a redirect still counts.\",\n        \"Add the redirect row the T009 table never had: head -n 1 2> <command document> must not set started.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"order\": 2,\n      \"advisory\": true,\n      \"name\": \"README offeredAs sentences\",\n      \"files\": [\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\"],\n      \"actions\": [\n        \"Change :123 to say a line written before the field existed holds no offeredAs, so a legacy line counts as before.\",\n        \"Move [--brief-only] out of the four-field sentence at :125, or say that the default backfill writes the four and the brief-only mode copies the offer fields as held.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"specSeed\": [\n    \"The routing-accuracy README is the document of record for the two writers; its stored-line sentence must distinguish a legacy line from a line the current writers produce.\",\n    \"The redirect guard in the transcript scorer should name the operator forms it accepts; the T009 table currently covers no redirect at all.\"\n  ],\n  \"planSeed\": [\n    \"Patch the redirect test in shellReadTargets and add a head -n 1 2> <doc> case to the startState table.\",\n    \"Edit README.md:123 to qualify the legacy line and README.md:125 to scope the four-field rewrite to the default backfill.\"\n  ],\n  \"findingClasses\": [\"correctness\", \"traceability\", \"maintainability\"],\n  \"affectedSurfacesSeed\": [\n    \"score-command-transcripts shell read and start detection\",\n    \"routing-accuracy README attribution section\",\n    \"run-command-behaviour backfill mode\"\n  ],\n  \"fixCompletenessRequired\": false\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\n\n### ARC4C-P2-001 — A `2>` or `&>` redirect target that names a command document still counts as a start\n\n- Severity: P2\n- Dimension: correctness\n- File: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:677`\n- Finding class: `correctness`\n- Evidence: `shellReadTargets` sets the redirect flag only for a word starting with `>` (`:677`). `2>` and `&>` do not match, so a target ending in `.md`, `.yaml` or `.yml` is pushed at `:687`. `readDocument` then returns true at `:922`.\n- Case: `head -n 1 2> .skilled/commands/create/readme.md` followed by a `Write`; the command reads stdin and writes stderr to the document, but `startState.started` is true.\n- Fix: recognize `2>`, `&>`, `2>>` and `&>>`; skip the target and continue scanning after it. Add the redirect row to the T009 table.\n- Scope proof: the scorer is a named verification surface in the 4c brief; the shell branch at `:922` is the T009 fix and `:677` is the redirect guard it relies on.\n- Affected surface hints: `startRate`, `startedOfOffered`, `loops`, `unsafe`, command documents, stderr redirects.\n- Disposition: advisory, P2.\n\n### ARC4C-P2-002 — The README says a stored run line holds no `offeredAs`, but both current writers store it\n\n- Severity: P2\n- Dimension: traceability\n- File: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:123`\n- Finding class: `traceability`\n- Evidence: `README.md:123` says \"A stored run line holds no `offeredAs`, so its offer counts as before.\" `command-offer.mjs:496` and `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1203` write the field; `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1471-1476` reads it to split `offeredAsPartner` from `offered`.\n- Case: a live line written at `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1201-1205` carries `offeredAs: \"partner\"`; `offerOf` counts it in `offeredAsPartner`, not in `offered`, while the README says a stored line holds no field and counts as before.\n- Fix: change the sentence to \"A run line written before the field existed holds no `offeredAs`, so its offer counts as before.\"\n- Scope proof: the README is the changed accuracy-runner path; both writers and the scorer are the brief's verification surfaces.\n- Affected surface hints: `offerOf`, `offeredAsPartner`, `offerFieldAbsent`, stored run logs, backfill.\n- Disposition: advisory, P2.\n\n### ARC4C-P2-003 — The runner row says `--brief-only` rewrites the four fields, but that mode copies the offer fields untouched\n\n- Severity: P2\n- Dimension: maintainability\n- File: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:125`\n- Finding class: `maintainability`\n- Evidence: `README.md:125` lists `[--brief-only]` in the sentence \"rewrites a finished log with `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs` and `briefDelivered`.\" `command-offer.mjs:489-490` copies the line and changes only `briefDelivered` and `briefBackfilled` when brief-only; the offer fields stay as held. `README.md:85` says the same.\n- Case: a legacy line with no offer fields, run through `--backfill --brief-only`; the output has `briefDelivered` and `briefBackfilled` but no `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy` or `offeredAs`, contradicting the runner row.\n- Fix: move `[--brief-only]` out of the four-field sentence, or qualify the sentence as the default backfill path.\n- Scope proof: the README is the changed accuracy-runner path; the brief-only branch is the writer the row describes.\n- Affected surface hints: `--brief-only`, backfill field list, `briefBackfilled`, legacy run logs.\n- Disposition: advisory, P2.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\n\n### P0 — none\n\n### P1 — none\n\n### P2 — advisory\n\n1. **Redirect operator parsing** (`score-command-transcripts.mjs`): recognize the `2>`, `&>`, `2>>`\n   and `&>>` forms, skip the target and keep scanning, and add the missing test row. This is one\n   guard and one test case.\n2. **README stored-line sentence** (`README.md:123`): qualify the legacy line so it does not claim\n   every stored line lacks `offeredAs`.\n3. **README brief-only clause** (`README.md:125`): scope the four-field rewrite to the default\n   backfill or move the flag out of the sentence.\n\nNone of these blocks the PASS finding verdict. Items 2 and 3 are doc-only and can fold into the\nphase 026 doc pass. Item 1 is a small parser guard in the scorer.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Spec Seed\n\n- The routing-accuracy README is the document of record for the two writers. Its stored-line\n  sentence must distinguish a line written before `offeredAs` existed from a line the current\n  writers produce.\n- The `--brief-only` mode copies every offer field exactly as held and recomputes only\n  `briefDelivered`. Any field-list sentence that includes the flag must say so.\n- The transcript scorer's redirect guard should name the operator forms it accepts. The T009 test\n  table covers `cat`, `rg`, an in-place `sed` and a heredoc, but no redirect.\n- A shell read of a command document is a start; a redirect target is not a read. The two rules are\n  independent and need separate cases.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Plan Seed\n\n- Add `2>`, `&>`, `2>>` and `&>>` to the redirect guard and skip only the target word; add a\n  start-state case for `head -n 1 2> <command document>` that expects `started: false`.\n- Edit `README.md:123` to name the legacy line and edit `README.md:125` to scope the four-field\n  rewrite to the default backfill.\n- Re-run the README's own three T030 string checks after the doc edits; no code or test change is\n  needed for the two doc findings.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Traceability Status\n\n### Core Protocols\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Notes |\n|----------|-------|--------|-------|\n| `spec_code` | core | partial | T006-T011 and T030 are `[x]` with evidence; the offeredAs writers, heredoc, shell read, Codex read and live holdout guard match. T009's redirect claim covers `>` only, and README `:123`/`:125` remain drift. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | partial | AC-003's `cat`, `rg`, in-place `sed` and heredoc inputs read as described; the brief's redirect input is not in that table. AC-010 is unmet for `:123` and the brief-only clause. `CHK-040` is met. |\n\n### Overlay Protocols\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Notes |\n|----------|-------|--------|-------|\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | notApplicable | No agent definition changed in this area. |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | notApplicable | The Codex reader is a shared session reader, not an agent definition; its resolved-path read is checked directly. |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | notApplicable | No feature-catalog page describes the changed accuracy-runner lines. |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | No playbook surface changed. |\n\n### AC_COVERAGE\n\n`exempt`. The review target's root folder has no `acceptance-criteria.md`; the phase children hold\ntheir own criteria, and this lineage's scope is the changed accuracy-runner files.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Deferred Items\n\n- **Phase 026 doc and code items.** The pair-doc shared-row sentence, the reserved `paired` arm name\n  and the dead `unscoredOnly` field are assigned to phase 026 by\n  `027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md:214`. They are recorded as the one search-debt row\n  `ARC4C-SL-009`, not re-reported as findings.\n- **The redirect parser edge is not deferred.** It is active as `ARC4C-P2-001`.\n- **No live per-runtime session was captured.** Runtime behavior is read from the fixed code, the\n  committed tests and the 027 evidence.\n- **The mention reader is the sibling lineage's surface.** `scorer-attach-close-4c` reads\n  `command-attach.ts`; this lineage raises no finding against it.\n\n---\n\n## Dimension Expansion Map\n\n- Completed pivots: none.\n- Failed pivots: none.\n- Audited overrides: none.\n- Swept directions: none. The two iterations covered correctness/security, then\n  traceability/maintainability.\n- Remaining frontier: none within the cap.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Search Ledger\n\n- `searchCoverage.requiredBugClasses`: `shell_command_parsing`, `start_detection`,\n  `heredoc_parsing`, `path_containment`, `holdout_publication`, `doc_code_drift`,\n  `doc_contradiction`, `checklist_evidence`, `deferred_scope`.\n- `searchCoverage.covered`: everything except `deferred_scope`.\n- `searchCoverage.ruledOut`: `heredoc_parsing`, `path_containment`, `holdout_publication`.\n- `searchCoverage.deferred`: `deferred_scope`.\n- `searchCoverage.blocked`: none.\n- `hasSearchDebt: true`. One row (`ARC4C-SL-009`) records the phase 026 deferral. The dashboard's\n  provisional verdict is CONDITIONAL on that debt; the finding-severity verdict is PASS, and the\n  cross-lineage merge recomputes from the findings registry.\n- `cleanSearchProof`: the heredoc end word, the Codex resolved read, the live holdout guard and the\n  two offeredAs writers each carry a direct-read ledger row with file:line evidence.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Audit Appendix\n\n### Convergence Summary\n\n| Iteration | Focus | P0/P1/P2 (new) | newFindingsRatio | Verdict |\n|-----------|-------|----------------|------------------|---------|\n| 1 | correctness and security | 0/0/1 | 1.0 | PASS |\n| 2 | traceability and maintainability | 0/0/2 | 0.6667 | PASS |\n\n- The rolling average of the two ratios is 0.8334, above the 0.10 threshold.\n- The cap is 2 and the second iteration still produced new findings, so the stop reason is\n  `maxIterationsReached`; convergence was not declared.\n- The release-readiness state is `in-progress`.\n\n### Coverage Summary\n\n- Dimensions: correctness, security, traceability, maintainability (4 of 4).\n- Files: the routing-accuracy README plus the two writers, the transcript scorer, the Codex reader\n  and the holdout test (6 of 6).\n- Active findings: 3 P2; no P0 or P1.\n\n### Ruled-Out Claims\n\n- `offeredAs` is still dropped by a writer.\n- A hyphen or dot heredoc end word is read as a command.\n- The Codex reader opens the caller's locator.\n- The holdout guard checks only the committed baseline.\n- A refusal or question over an or-list carries a command (sibling surface; read as context).\n\n### Sources Reviewed\n\n- `review/review-brief-4c.txt`, `review/review-scope-4c.txt`, `review/verify-4/report.md`.\n- `027-review-pass-four-remediation/scratch/review-rounds.txt`, `spec.md:204-238`,\n  `tasks.md:84-110`.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md`,\n  `command-offer.mjs`, `run-command-behaviour.mjs`, `score-command-transcripts.mjs`.\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/codex.mjs`,\n  `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts`.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` (context only).\n\n### Cross-Reference Appendix\n\nCore protocols: `spec_code` partial, `checklist_evidence` partial. Overlay protocols:\n`skill_agent`, `agent_cross_runtime`, `feature_catalog_code` and `playbook_capability`\nnotApplicable.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-close-4c/review-report.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-close-4c/review-report.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-close-4c/review-report.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Report: Command Surfacing Build, Pass Four (accuracy-runner closeout lineage)\\n\\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder)\\n- Pass: the closing round of review pass four, on the fix range `48f03b5013..868b185e76`.\\n- Lineage: `accuracy-runner-close-4c`, area `accuracy-runner`, run\\n  `fanout-accuracy-runner-close-4c-1794682797954-pcdanq`, executor `cli-opencode`\\n  `opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash` at reasoning effort max.\\n- Reviewed scope: the one accuracy-runner path in `review/review-scope-4c.txt` (the routing-accuracy\\n  `README.md`) plus the six code and test surfaces the brief names as verification checks: the two\\n  run-log writers, the transcript scorer, the Codex reader and the holdout guard.\\n- Inputs to this synthesis: the two iteration narratives, the two delta files, the lineage registry\\n  (3 active P2 findings), the strategy and the dashboard.\\n- Cross-area boundary: `lib/command-attach.ts`, the scorer fusion, the recommend handler and the\\n  feature docs belong to `scorer-attach-close-4c`. This lineage read the mention reader only as\\n  context and raises no finding against it.\\n- Iteration cap: 2 of 2. The loop stopped at the cap; convergence was not declared.\\n- Operator review focus: Closing round of review pass four of command surfacing. FIRST read and\\n  follow `review-brief-4c.txt`; it names the scope file, the commit range, which files the lineage\\n  reviews and the checks. HOLDOUT RULE: never open `command-prompts.jsonl` or\\n  `holdout-prompts.jsonl` except through `jq 'del(.prompt)'`, never run `git diff`, `show` or\\n  `log -p` over a path that includes `command-prompts.jsonl` without the pathspec\\n  `:(exclude)**/command-prompts.jsonl`, and never print a prompt whose split is holdout. The\\n  reviewer changes no code and writes only inside its lineage folder.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Executive Summary\\n\\n- **Finding verdict: PASS.** No P0 and no P1 finding is active.\\n- **hasAdvisories: true.** Three P2 findings remain active: one parser edge and two documentation\\n  drifts.\\n- **Active counts:** P0 0, P1 0, P2 3.\\n- **The 4b accuracy-runner P2s are fixed.** `README.md:76` now says four fields, `:125` lists\\n  `offeredAs`, and `:70` names the head-moved line's four-field exception. No \\\"three fields\\\" string\\n  remains.\\n- **Both run-log writers keep `offeredAs`.** The backfill writes it at `command-offer.mjs:496`, the\\n  live turn spreads `offerLineFields` at `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1203`, and the scorer reads it\\n  at `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1471-1476`.\\n- **The other brief checks hold.** A `cat` of a command document counts as a start; `rg`, an\\n  in-place `sed` and a heredoc line do not. A heredoc end word with a hyphen or a dot closes. The\\n  Codex reader opens `storePath`, the file containment resolved. The holdout guard checks the live\\n  capture as well as the committed baseline.\\n- **The new P2 parser edge.** `shellReadTargets` recognizes only a word starting with `>` as a\\n  redirect, so a `2>` or `&>` target that names a command document is counted as a read and, through\\n  `readDocument`, as a start (`score-command-transcripts.mjs:677,922`).\\n- **The two new P2 doc drifts.** `README.md:123` still says a stored run line holds no `offeredAs`,\\n  which the fixed writers made false. `README.md:125` puts `[--brief-only]` inside a sentence that\\n  promises the four-field rewrite, which that mode does not perform; `README.md:85` states the\\n  correct behavior.\\n- **Search debt.** One deferred scope row records the phase 026 items (pair-doc shared row,\\n  reserved `paired` arm name, dead `unscoredOnly` field). The dashboard's provisional verdict is\\n  CONDITIONAL on that debt; the finding-severity verdict is PASS, and the cross-lineage merge\\n  recomputes from the findings registry.\\n- **Holdout hygiene:** no holdout prompt text was read or printed. Corpus access was limited to the\\n  code and the committed test, and no prompt value is used in a finding or report sentence.\\n- **Release readiness:** `in-progress`. The cap was reached; no convergence event was recorded.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Planning Trigger\\n\\nNo plan is required for the PASS finding verdict. The three P2s are advisory: two documentation\\ncorrections and one small parser guard. They do not block release. The phase 026 deferral is\\nrecorded as search debt, not as a new finding.\\n\\n```json Planning Packet\\n{\\n  \\\"triggered\\\": false,\\n  \\\"triggerReason\\\": \\\"PASS with three advisory P2 findings; no P0 or P1 remains.\\\",\\n  \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n  \\\"dashboardVerdict\\\": \\\"CONDITIONAL\\\",\\n  \\\"hasAdvisories\\\": true,\\n  \\\"hasSearchDebt\\\": true,\\n  \\\"counts\\\": { \\\"p0\\\": 0, \\\"p1\\\": 0, \\\"p2\\\": 3, \\\"active\\\": 3, \\\"iterations\\\": 2 },\\n  \\\"activeFindings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"ARC4C-P2-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"A 2> or &> redirect target that names a command document still counts as a start\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:677\\\",\\n      \\\"findingClass\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"advisory\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"ARC4C-P2-002\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"The README says a stored run line holds no offeredAs, but both current writers store it\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:123\\\",\\n      \\\"findingClass\\\": \\\"traceability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"advisory\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"ARC4C-P2-003\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"The runner row says --brief-only rewrites the four fields, but that mode copies the offer fields untouched\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:125\\\",\\n      \\\"findingClass\\\": \\\"maintainability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"advisory\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"remediationWorkstreams\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"order\\\": 1,\\n      \\\"advisory\\\": true,\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Redirect operator parsing\\\",\\n      \\\"files\\\": [\\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs\\\"],\\n      \\\"actions\\\": [\\n        \\\"Recognize 2>, &>, 2>> and &>> as redirect operators in shellReadTargets, not only a word starting with >.\\\",\\n        \\\"Skip the redirect target rather than every later word, so a real read after a redirect still counts.\\\",\\n        \\\"Add the redirect row the T009 table never had: head -n 1 2> <command document> must not set started.\\\"\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"order\\\": 2,\\n      \\\"advisory\\\": true,\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"README offeredAs sentences\\\",\\n      \\\"files\\\": [\\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\\\"],\\n      \\\"actions\\\": [\\n        \\\"Change :123 to say a line written before the field existed holds no offeredAs, so a legacy line counts as before.\\\",\\n        \\\"Move [--brief-only] out of the four-field sentence at :125, or say that the default backfill writes the four and the brief-only mode copies the offer fields as held.\\\"\\n      ]\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"specSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\"The routing-accuracy README is the document of record for the two writers; its stored-line sentence must distinguish a legacy line from a line the current writers produce.\\\",\\n    \\\"The redirect guard in the transcript scorer should name the operator forms it accepts; the T009 table currently covers no redirect at all.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"planSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\"Patch the redirect test in shellReadTargets and add a head -n 1 2> <doc> case to the startState table.\\\",\\n    \\\"Edit README.md:123 to qualify the legacy line and README.md:125 to scope the four-field rewrite to the default backfill.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"findingClasses\\\": [\\\"correctness\\\", \\\"traceability\\\", \\\"maintainability\\\"],\\n  \\\"affectedSurfacesSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\"score-command-transcripts shell read and start detection\\\",\\n    \\\"routing-accuracy README attribution section\\\",\\n    \\\"run-command-behaviour backfill mode\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"fixCompletenessRequired\\\": false\\n}\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\\n\\n### ARC4C-P2-001 — A `2>` or `&>` redirect target that names a command document still counts as a start\\n\\n- Severity: P2\\n- Dimension: correctness\\n- File: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:677`\\n- Finding class: `correctness`\\n- Evidence: `shellReadTargets` sets the redirect flag only for a word starting with `>` (`:677`). `2>` and `&>` do not match, so a target ending in `.md`, `.yaml` or `.yml` is pushed at `:687`. `readDocument` then returns true at `:922`.\\n- Case: `head -n 1 2> .skilled/commands/create/readme.md` followed by a `Write`; the command reads stdin and writes stderr to the document, but `startState.started` is true.\\n- Fix: recognize `2>`, `&>`, `2>>` and `&>>`; skip the target and continue scanning after it. Add the redirect row to the T009 table.\\n- Scope proof: the scorer is a named verification surface in the 4c brief; the shell branch at `:922` is the T009 fix and `:677` is the redirect guard it relies on.\\n- Affected surface hints: `startRate`, `startedOfOffered`, `loops`, `unsafe`, command documents, stderr redirects.\\n- Disposition: advisory, P2.\\n\\n### ARC4C-P2-002 — The README says a stored run line holds no `offeredAs`, but both current writers store it\\n\\n- Severity: P2\\n- Dimension: traceability\\n- File: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:123`\\n- Finding class: `traceability`\\n- Evidence: `README.md:123` says \\\"A stored run line holds no `offeredAs`, so its offer counts as before.\\\" `command-offer.mjs:496` and `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1203` write the field; `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1471-1476` reads it to split `offeredAsPartner` from `offered`.\\n- Case: a live line written at `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1201-1205` carries `offeredAs: \\\"partner\\\"`; `offerOf` counts it in `offeredAsPartner`, not in `offered`, while the README says a stored line holds no field and counts as before.\\n- Fix: change the sentence to \\\"A run line written before the field existed holds no `offeredAs`, so its offer counts as before.\\\"\\n- Scope proof: the README is the changed accuracy-runner path; both writers and the scorer are the brief's verification surfaces.\\n- Affected surface hints: `offerOf`, `offeredAsPartner`, `offerFieldAbsent`, stored run logs, backfill.\\n- Disposition: advisory, P2.\\n\\n### ARC4C-P2-003 — The runner row says `--brief-only` rewrites the four fields, but that mode copies the offer fields untouched\\n\\n- Severity: P2\\n- Dimension: maintainability\\n- File: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:125`\\n- Finding class: `maintainability`\\n- Evidence: `README.md:125` lists `[--brief-only]` in the sentence \\\"rewrites a finished log with `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs` and `briefDelivered`.\\\" `command-offer.mjs:489-490` copies the line and changes only `briefDelivered` and `briefBackfilled` when brief-only; the offer fields stay as held. `README.md:85` says the same.\\n- Case: a legacy line with no offer fields, run through `--backfill --brief-only`; the output has `briefDelivered` and `briefBackfilled` but no `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy` or `offeredAs`, contradicting the runner row.\\n- Fix: move `[--brief-only]` out of the four-field sentence, or qualify the sentence as the default backfill path.\\n- Scope proof: the README is the changed accuracy-runner path; the brief-only branch is the writer the row describes.\\n- Affected surface hints: `--brief-only`, backfill field list, `briefBackfilled`, legacy run logs.\\n- Disposition: advisory, P2.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\\n\\n### P0 — none\\n\\n### P1 — none\\n\\n### P2 — advisory\\n\\n1. **Redirect operator parsing** (`score-command-transcripts.mjs`): recognize the `2>`, `&>`, `2>>`\\n   and `&>>` forms, skip the target and keep scanning, and add the missing test row. This is one\\n   guard and one test case.\\n2. **README stored-line sentence** (`README.md:123`): qualify the legacy line so it does not claim\\n   every stored line lacks `offeredAs`.\\n3. **README brief-only clause** (`README.md:125`): scope the four-field rewrite to the default\\n   backfill or move the flag out of the sentence.\\n\\nNone of these blocks the PASS finding verdict. Items 2 and 3 are doc-only and can fold into the\\nphase 026 doc pass. Item 1 is a small parser guard in the scorer.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. Spec Seed\\n\\n- The routing-accuracy README is the document of record for the two writers. Its stored-line\\n  sentence must distinguish a line written before `offeredAs` existed from a line the current\\n  writers produce.\\n- The `--brief-only` mode copies every offer field exactly as held and recomputes only\\n  `briefDelivered`. Any field-list sentence that includes the flag must say so.\\n- The transcript scorer's redirect guard should name the operator forms it accepts. The T009 test\\n  table covers `cat`, `rg`, an in-place `sed` and a heredoc, but no redirect.\\n- A shell read of a command document is a start; a redirect target is not a read. The two rules are\\n  independent and need separate cases.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Plan Seed\\n\\n- Add `2>`, `&>`, `2>>` and `&>>` to the redirect guard and skip only the target word; add a\\n  start-state case for `head -n 1 2> <command document>` that expects `started: false`.\\n- Edit `README.md:123` to name the legacy line and edit `README.md:125` to scope the four-field\\n  rewrite to the default backfill.\\n- Re-run the README's own three T030 string checks after the doc edits; no code or test change is\\n  needed for the two doc findings.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Traceability Status\\n\\n### Core Protocols\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Notes |\\n|----------|-------|--------|-------|\\n| `spec_code` | core | partial | T006-T011 and T030 are `[x]` with evidence; the offeredAs writers, heredoc, shell read, Codex read and live holdout guard match. T009's redirect claim covers `>` only, and README `:123`/`:125` remain drift. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | partial | AC-003's `cat`, `rg`, in-place `sed` and heredoc inputs read as described; the brief's redirect input is not in that table. AC-010 is unmet for `:123` and the brief-only clause. `CHK-040` is met. |\\n\\n### Overlay Protocols\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Notes |\\n|----------|-------|--------|-------|\\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | notApplicable | No agent definition changed in this area. |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | notApplicable | The Codex reader is a shared session reader, not an agent definition; its resolved-path read is checked directly. |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | notApplicable | No feature-catalog page describes the changed accuracy-runner lines. |\\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | No playbook surface changed. |\\n\\n### AC_COVERAGE\\n\\n`exempt`. The review target's root folder has no `acceptance-criteria.md`; the phase children hold\\ntheir own criteria, and this lineage's scope is the changed accuracy-runner files.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Deferred Items\\n\\n- **Phase 026 doc and code items.** The pair-doc shared-row sentence, the reserved `paired` arm name\\n  and the dead `unscoredOnly` field are assigned to phase 026 by\\n  `027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md:214`. They are recorded as the one search-debt row\\n  `ARC4C-SL-009`, not re-reported as findings.\\n- **The redirect parser edge is not deferred.** It is active as `ARC4C-P2-001`.\\n- **No live per-runtime session was captured.** Runtime behavior is read from the fixed code, the\\n  committed tests and the 027 evidence.\\n- **The mention reader is the sibling lineage's surface.** `scorer-attach-close-4c` reads\\n  `command-attach.ts`; this lineage raises no finding against it.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Dimension Expansion Map\\n\\n- Completed pivots: none.\\n- Failed pivots: none.\\n- Audited overrides: none.\\n- Swept directions: none. The two iterations covered correctness/security, then\\n  traceability/maintainability.\\n- Remaining frontier: none within the cap.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Search Ledger\\n\\n- `searchCoverage.requiredBugClasses`: `shell_command_parsing`, `start_detection`,\\n  `heredoc_parsing`, `path_containment`, `holdout_publication`, `doc_code_drift`,\\n  `doc_contradiction`, `checklist_evidence`, `deferred_scope`.\\n- `searchCoverage.covered`: everything except `deferred_scope`.\\n- `searchCoverage.ruledOut`: `heredoc_parsing`, `path_containment`, `holdout_publication`.\\n- `searchCoverage.deferred`: `deferred_scope`.\\n- `searchCoverage.blocked`: none.\\n- `hasSearchDebt: true`. One row (`ARC4C-SL-009`) records the phase 026 deferral. The dashboard's\\n  provisional verdict is CONDITIONAL on that debt; the finding-severity verdict is PASS, and the\\n  cross-lineage merge recomputes from the findings registry.\\n- `cleanSearchProof`: the heredoc end word, the Codex resolved read, the live holdout guard and the\\n  two offeredAs writers each carry a direct-read ledger row with file:line evidence.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Audit Appendix\\n\\n### Convergence Summary\\n\\n| Iteration | Focus | P0/P1/P2 (new) | newFindingsRatio | Verdict |\\n|-----------|-------|----------------|------------------|---------|\\n| 1 | correctness and security | 0/0/1 | 1.0 | PASS |\\n| 2 | traceability and maintainability | 0/0/2 | 0.6667 | PASS |\\n\\n- The rolling average of the two ratios is 0.8334, above the 0.10 threshold.\\n- The cap is 2 and the second iteration still produced new findings, so the stop reason is\\n  `maxIterationsReached`; convergence was not declared.\\n- The release-readiness state is `in-progress`.\\n\\n### Coverage Summary\\n\\n- Dimensions: correctness, security, traceability, maintainability (4 of 4).\\n- Files: the routing-accuracy README plus the two writers, the transcript scorer, the Codex reader\\n  and the holdout test (6 of 6).\\n- Active findings: 3 P2; no P0 or P1.\\n\\n### Ruled-Out Claims\\n\\n- `offeredAs` is still dropped by a writer.\\n- A hyphen or dot heredoc end word is read as a command.\\n- The Codex reader opens the caller's locator.\\n- The holdout guard checks only the committed baseline.\\n- A refusal or question over an or-list carries a command (sibling surface; read as context).\\n\\n### Sources Reviewed\\n\\n- `review/review-brief-4c.txt`, `review/review-scope-4c.txt`, `review/verify-4/report.md`.\\n- `027-review-pass-four-remediation/scratch/review-rounds.txt`, `spec.md:204-238`,\\n  `tasks.md:84-110`.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md`,\\n  `command-offer.mjs`, `run-command-behaviour.mjs`, `score-command-transcripts.mjs`.\\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/codex.mjs`,\\n  `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts`.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` (context only).\\n\\n### Cross-Reference Appendix\\n\\nCore protocols: `spec_code` partial, `checklist_evidence` partial. Overlay protocols:\\n`skill_agent`, `agent_cross_runtime`, `feature_catalog_code` and `playbook_capability`\\nnotApplicable.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-close-4c/review-report.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794684226663,"end":1794684266396}}}}
